  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"ahri","win":["Ahri","Ahri","Ahri","Ahri","Ahri","Azir","Azir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Ahri's Charm-into-full-combo is her kill pattern here; Charm stops on the first thing it touches, so a minion between you eats it — she must angle around your wave first."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ahri 6 gives her a true kill threat with Orb-Charm-R-Orb, and she can dash to you through your own wall of soldiers with Spirit Rush, so your Shurima's Legacy wall doesn't fully protect you."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Once you finish Liandry's/Shojin your poke and wave clear both spike hard, and your soldiers start doing enough chip damage that Ahri has to respect the zone instead of freely diving it."},{"when":"Late","text":"Your 5-man ultimate-enabling Emperor's Divide plus full-build soldier waveclear wins teamfights outright, while Ahri's damage falls off relative to your scaling and she becomes a pick-threat only."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive the all-in windows around 3-5 without overextending for cs","Hold soldiers back as zoning tools rather than pushing recklessly","Play for scaling — this matchup rewards patience into 2-item Azir"],"foe":["Land Charm through minion clutter or fog to lock you for the follow-up","Snowball the level 3 and level 6 all-ins before you can itemize","Deny your farm with orb harass so you never reach your power spikes"]},"early":"Ahri's Orb of Deception poke chips your HP every time you step up to last-hit, and she's looking for any Charm angle through your soldiers to chain into a full combo kill — you're mostly playing for CS and waiting out her cooldowns rather than contesting trades. Track Ahri Charm (E): 12s flat — it stops movement abilities, so it freezes Shifting Sands mid-dash. Step up only after she misses it.","mid":"Level 6 is genuinely dangerous since her Spirit Rush lets her jump your wall and Charm you regardless of soldier placement, so hug your tower until you have summoner spells up; from there your own 6 and Shurima's Legacy let you start punishing her if she misses Charm.","late":"With Liandry's or Shojin online your soldiers threaten real all-in damage and your ultimate becomes a teamfight-winning zone control tool, so by 2+ items you should be pushing waves and using Emperor's Divide to separate Ahri from her team rather than dueling her 1v1.","whys":["Ahri's Orb of Deception poke outranges your early soldier harass and she can punish CS attempts freely","Her Charm range and follow-up combo threaten a kill the moment you misstep near minions","Continued poke and Charm setup pressure keep her ahead through the mid-wave phase","Ahri still holds the edge as her mobility around soldiers remains a threat into level 6","Her Spirit Rush plus full combo is a genuine all-in kill window right at 6","Your item spikes let your soldier damage and waveclear start overpowering her","Your scaling ultimate and 2-item soldier pressure flip the matchup decisively late"]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"akali","win":["Akali","Akali","Skill","Skill","Skill","Akali","Azir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Akali's Five Point Strike into Twilight Shroud lets her stack Assassin's Mark and dive your soldier zone with impunity since her mark damage ignores most of your soldier positioning."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Akali 6 (Perfect Execution) is a hard all-in threat: the recast dashes again and executes, so it chases you through soldier walls whenever you are pushed up with Emperor's Divide down."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your first item (Shojin or Liandry's) plus consistent soldier spacing lets you finally punish her for entering Shroud, since your damage-over-time and R combo threaten to burst her before her Shroud heal offsets it."},{"when":"Late","text":"Your scaling wave clear and R zone control dominate teamfights, while Akali's damage plateaus and she's forced into pure pick mode rather than a straight duel."}],"wants":{"you":["Play passive around Shroud and don't walk soldiers into melee range for free","Ward and ping her R engages onto your carries in the mid-game","Rush Shojin to make your combo threaten her before her Shroud sustain kicks in"],"foe":["Stack Assassin's Mark with Q/W then finish in Shroud where you can't see her","All-in off 6 while you're overextended pushing the wave","Snowball early kills to invalidate your late-game item scaling"]},"early":"Akali's Twilight Shroud completely nullifies your soldier auto-attacks and Q pokes since she can just step into it and vanish, so she wins straight trades in the fog and you should default to farming with W and Arise! from max range rather than engaging. Track Akali Twilight Shroud (W): 20s at rank 1, free to cast — she is untargetable inside, so hold Q and R until she exits or the shroud ends.","mid":"Level 6 is her spike — Perfect Execution's second cast chases you down even behind soldiers — so play it safe until your own ultimate is up, at which point Emperor's Divide can shove her out of all-in range and punish her dash timing.","late":"Once you have Shojin or Liandry's your combo (soldiers + Q + R) threatens to punish her Shroud entries outright, and by full build your wave clear and 5-man R utility outclass her single-target assassination, forcing her into isolated pick attempts instead of laning duels.","whys":["Five Point Strike out-trades a single soldier at level 1, and her energy refills faster than your mana","Level 2 adds Shuriken Flip: she flips in on the soldier, Qs, and walks out before two soldiers pay it back","Both sides trade evenly here since good Q positioning from you can punish her Shroud entries just as much as she punishes you","Even matchup continues as her jungle-assisted all-ins and your ability to zone with soldiers roughly cancel out","Emperor's Divide knocks her out of Perfect Execution, so your 6 answers her 6 and the dive stops working","Her Perfect Execution all-in stays a real kill threat if you are caught out of position near her Shroud","Your late-game item scaling and R zone control put you clearly ahead in the final phase"]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"akshan","win":["Akshan","Akshan","Akshan","Akshan","Akshan","Skill","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Akshan's Avengerang poke plus his passive camo from bushes lets him harass you for free while your soldiers can't punish a target he can just stealth away from behind a ward or minion."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Comeuppance (R) threatens a long-range execute on you or your allies through walls, meaning any soldier engage you commit to can get punished from off-screen."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Even with Shojin or Liandry's online, Akshan's mobility (E hookshot on terrain/allies) and stealth uptime let him disengage from your combos before you get full value, keeping the matchup uncomfortable."},{"when":"Late","text":"Akshan's hypercarry AD scaling and pick potential with R stay relevant, but your 5-man R and wave clear finally give you enough map presence to offset his pick threat if you play around your team."}],"wants":{"you":["Avoid overextending into brush where his camouflage passive punishes vision mistakes","Group soldiers to threaten burst before he can stealth away","Play for teamfight utility with your ultimate rather than 1v1 trades"],"foe":["Poke with Avengerang from stealth angles you can't ward in time","Look for global R picks on overextended soldiers or allies","Out-scale you as an AD hypercarry into a 1v9 late game"]},"early":"Akshan's Avengerang harass paired with his camouflage-in-brush passive makes him nearly impossible to punish cleanly, since he can poke and vanish before your soldiers land meaningful damage, so you're stuck farming carefully under constant chip pressure. Track Akshan Heroic Swing (E): 18s at rank 1, 12s at rank 5 — he is knocked off it by colliding with a champion, so step into the swing line.","mid":"His kit doesn't get materially worse for you at 6 — Comeuppance threatens executions on soldiers or allies from absurd range, so grouped or overextended play gets punished hard, and his mobility via E lets him reposition around your zone control at will.","late":"Akshan continues to scale as an AD hypercarry with global pick potential from his ultimate, so even with your items online you need to play this as a teamfight-control matchup rather than a lane-kill matchup, using Emperor's Divide to protect carries from his R rather than trying to out-duel him.","whys":["Akshan's poke-and-stealth combo wins early trades cleanly with no good punish available to you","His camouflage passive keeps him ahead as he continues to harass without taking risk","Sustained poke and safe stealth angles maintain his lane advantage through mid lane","The gap holds as his mobility answers your soldier zoning attempts","Comeuppance gives him a long-range execute threat that keeps him favoured at 6","Item timings don't close the gap since his kit counters your combo execution directly","His AD scaling and global R pick potential keep him ahead into the late game"]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"anivia","win":["Azir","Azir","Azir","Skill","Anivia","Azir","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"You out-range and out-wave Anivia early since your soldiers push and poke faster than her Frostbite/Flash Frost combo can land consistently, letting you shove and threaten roams."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Neither ultimate creates a clean kill window here — her Glacial Storm zones you out but your R can reposition soldiers around it, so this phase is closer to a stalemate than a clear spike for either side."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Anivia's Crystallize (W) becomes a real threat once she can punish your positioning, with Rebirth keeping her alive through your poke, letting her wall-combo you for a big trade if you overextend."},{"when":"Late","text":"Your scaling wave clear and 5-man R utility outclass her one-dimensional zone control, and your soldiers can force her to use Rebirth's egg form defensively rather than offensively."}],"wants":{"you":["Punish her low mobility early with soldier zoning and aggressive wave pushes","Bait Flash Frost rather than eating it directly since it's her main engage/poke tool","Play around her wall placement in mid-late skirmishes to avoid getting boxed in"],"foe":["Land Flash Frost into Frostbite for a big early poke exchange","Use Crystallize (W) to wall you off from allies or escape routes for a punish","Stack Rebirth sustain to survive your late soldier pressure and out-zone with Glacial Storm"]},"early":"Anivia's early game is clunky without her wall combo fully online, and your soldier pressure lets you shove waves and zone her from farm safely, so you should be aggressively punishing her lower mobility and forcing bad Flash Frost trades. Track Flash Frost is 11s at rank 1 and travels 1075 units slowly — sidestep it and Frostbite's 4s never doubles. You out-range and out-wave Anivia early since your soldiers push and poke faster than her Frostbite/Flash Frost combo can land consistently, letting you shove and threaten roams.","mid":"Level 6 doesn't swing hard either way — her Glacial Storm zones effectively but your R repositioning keeps you safe from getting boxed in, so this phase is about careful play around her wall rather than an all-in window for either of you.","late":"Anivia's Rebirth sustain gets dangerous if she reaches a big mid-late item spike and can wall-combo you in skirmishes for a huge trade, so respect her Crystallize placement, but by full build your wave clear and ultimate utility should let you close out fights before she can lock down the fight.","whys":["Your soldier pressure and range advantage let you dominate her clunky early laning phase","Continued wave pressure and poke keep you ahead as she struggles to punish your positioning","Your zoning and farm lead carry into a comfortable mid-lane advantage","Neither side has a clean edge here — her zone control and your repositioning largely cancel out","Glacial Storm at 6 is a 60-mana toggle that slows and doubles Frostbite on anything inside it — your soldiers have to stand in the storm to hit her, so level 6 is hers.","You reassert control thanks to superior scaling and wave clear at your item spike","Late-game skirmishes are close since her zone control can still punish greedy positioning even as you outscale"]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"annie","win":["Annie","Annie","Annie","Annie","Annie","Azir","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Annie's passive Pyromania stun procs off her Q/W poke and threatens to lock you down through your own soldiers for a follow-up trade you can't contest at range."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Tibbers plus a stacked stun is a full kill combo — she can flash-stun-Tibbers you even behind your soldier wall since the stun bypasses positioning entirely."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Once Liandry's or Shojin comes online your soldier damage and poke finally out-trade her burst, and your extra range lets you punish her for walking up to stack Pyromania."},{"when":"Late","text":"Your wave clear and 5-man R zone control dominate teamfights while Annie's single burst combo, though still dangerous, gets kited by soldier positioning and peel from your team."}],"wants":{"you":["Track her stun stacks (watch for the Pyromania icon) before engaging or extending trades","Avoid clustering with allies near her Tibbers threat range","Rush your first item to flip the poke war in your favour"],"foe":["Stack Pyromania then chain stun into Tibbers for a full burst kill","Flash-stun picks on overextended soldiers or squishies","Zone your farm with Disintegrate poke and force bad trades"]},"early":"Annie's stun-into-Tibbers combo is a constant kill threat every time her passive is up, and her Disintegrate poke chips you for free while you're trying to farm with soldiers, so you need to track her stun stacks closely and avoid extending trades until you can see it's down. Track Annie Pyromania: her fourth spell stuns, and Disintegrate is a 4s refresh — she can stock it on the wave in eight seconds of last-hitting.","mid":"Level 6 is her scariest window — Tibbers on top of a stun is close to a guaranteed kill if you're caught even slightly out of position, so play max-range and don't contest pushes until your own item spike gives you the tools to punish her aggression.","late":"With Shojin or Liandry's finished your poke and wave clear start winning the ranged war outright, and by full build your R utility and soldier zoning in teamfights outclass her single burst combo as long as your team peels the engage.","whys":["Annie spawns with Pyromania stocked, so her level 1 stun into Disintegrate is live before your soldiers are","Her passive stun window continues to punish any aggressive play from you","Sustained poke and burst threat keep her ahead through the mid-wave phase","A stocked stun into Disintegrate and Incinerate still out-bursts a soldier trade — drag Qs through her only when the glow is gone","Her all-in burst combo stays dangerous and defines this phase in her favour","Your item spike lets your poke and range finally outtrade her burst combo","Your scaling wave clear and ultimate utility put you ahead once fights become 5v5"]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"aurelionsol","win":["Skill","Skill","Azir","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Your soldiers zone and out-range his Breath of Light channel completely, since at 750 range he must walk toward your soldier zone to hold the beam on you at all."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Aurelion Sol's Falling Star stuns where it lands, so sidestep the marker, and your own R answers the follow-up before Singularity can drag you into the black hole's centre."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your Shojin/Liandry's spike widens the gap further since your soldier waveclear and poke chip him down faster than his orbiting star can punish you for stepping up."},{"when":"Late","text":"This becomes closer to a coinflip — Stardust permanently improves every ability, so his Breath of Light and Singularity zone your whole team off objectives, and positioning matters far more than raw stats."}],"wants":{"you":["Push waves early to deny the Stardust his whole kit permanently scales on","Bait his Astral Flight (W) engage/escape before committing your own R","Play around vision late since his star scaling can punish blind engages hard"],"foe":["Farm safely under tower to bank Stardust for late-game poke","Look for Astral Flight flank engages once Stardust is stacked","Zone your team off objectives with a Stardust-scaled Singularity late"]},"early":"Aurelion Sol is clunky and immobile early with no Stardust banked, so your soldier zoning and range advantage let you push waves and starve his farm, denying the stacking that his entire kit depends on. Track Aurelion Sol Astral Flight (W): 22s at rank 1 — it is his reposition and his escape, and Breath of Light loses its cooldown while he flies, so fight him grounded.","mid":"Level 6 doesn't change much in his favour — his ultimate is slow and telegraphed enough that you can reposition soldiers around it, and your own R gives you an escape or counter-engage tool his kit struggles to answer.","late":"Your item spike widens the early lead further since your soldiers now punish any approach he makes, keeping his Stardust low and his damage output well behind yours through the mid-game.","whys":["Your soldier zoning and range shut down his weak, unscaled early kit completely","Continued wave pressure keeps him starved of the stacks his kit needs to function","Shifting Sands is your out at 22s and he has no way to punish greedier soldier placements — Breath of Light is a channel, and a soldier drag-through forces him to move and drop it.","Your range and mobility advantage keep you ahead as his kit remains reactive","His ultimate is slow enough to dodge and your own R answers his engage attempts","Your consistent farming and zoning have banked a lead that's hard for him to claw back","A fully-stacked Aurelion Sol zones entire teams with Singularity, making late fights closer to even and skill-dependent"]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"aurora","win":["Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Azir","Azir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Aurora's The Weirding poke plus Spirit Abjuration's healing chips you down every time you step up to farm, and her 22s hop dodges your soldier zoning outright."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds gives her a hard engage/disengage and a teleport across its own zone, letting her all-in or reset a fight on her terms."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Even with Shojin or Liandry's, her mobility and poke uptime keep the lane uncomfortable, since she can still dash away from your combo before you get full value."},{"when":"Late","text":"Your scaling wave clear and 5-man ultimate finally give you the tools to zone her out of fights, though her mobility still makes her hard to pin down cleanly."}],"wants":{"you":["Play patiently and avoid overextending into her poke range","Track her R cooldown before committing to trades or engages","Group your soldiers to threaten burst damage before she can dash away"],"foe":["Poke relentlessly with Q while dashing in and out of soldier range","Use Between Worlds to dodge your engage or reset fights on her terms","Snowball early poke damage into a lane kill before your items come online"]},"early":"Aurora's ranged poke and dash mobility let her chip you down while dodging your soldier zoning entirely, so you're mostly playing defensively and looking to farm safely rather than contest trades directly. Track Aurora Across the Veil (W): 22s at rank 1 — she lands invisible, so the hop is both her escape and her setup. Aurora's The Weirding poke plus Spirit Abjuration's healing chips you down every time you step up to farm, and her 22s hop dodges your soldier zoning outright.","mid":"Her ultimate gives her a strong engage or disengage tool that can slip past your R positioning, so respect her all-in windows around 6 and don't get caught overextended when Between Worlds is up.","late":"Even once your items come online her mobility keeps the matchup uncomfortable in isolated skirmishes, but your wave clear and ultimate utility in full 5v5 fights let you zone her out and mitigate her poke advantage.","whys":["Aurora's poke and mobility win the early trading war cleanly against your slower zoning tools","Her continued dash-poke pattern keeps her ahead as you struggle to punish her aggression","Sustained poke damage and safe engages maintain her lane advantage into the late-early game","The pattern holds as her range and mobility continue to outclass your positioning tools","Her ultimate engage/disengage tool keeps her ahead through this all-in-capable window","Your first item gives you real combo threat, flipping the trading dynamic in your favour","Your scaling wave clear and R utility put you ahead once teamfights become the priority"]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"brand","win":["Brand","Brand","Brand","Skill","Skill","Skill","Azir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Brand can hard-zone your soldier casts with Sear-Pillar-Conflagration combos that chunk 50%+ if you're caught out of position near minions."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Pyroclasm bounces five times and stacks Blaze to max, so his level 6 all-in is Sear stun into a detonation you cannot walk out of."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Once Nashor's Tooth is finished your soldier autos out-trade him: he has 8s of cooldowns against your continuous soldier DPS."},{"when":"Late","text":"Your late-game teamfighting with Emperor's Divide and full soldier walls wins outright — he has no answer to a full-build Azir ultimate."}],"wants":{"you":["Farm from max range behind soldiers, never let Sear line you up with minions behind you","Push to force his roams to be less impactful, then hold prio for turret plates","Rush Nashor's Tooth, then Rabadon's — survive to the two-item spike"],"foe":["Land Sear off cooldown to set up Conflagration/Pillar combos","Zone you off minions near his own turret with passive stacks","Look for all-in windows the moment Sear connects for a stun-into-burst kill"]},"early":"Brand's Sear-Pillar-Conflagration combo threatens 40-50% of your health from range, and because you have to walk soldiers forward to farm you're constantly in his passive splash radius — respect his cooldown and back off minions when Sear is up. Track Sear is 8s at rank 1 and 6s at rank 5, and it only stuns while Blaze is on you — so after his W or E lands, the stun line is the one dodge that matters.","mid":"Once you hit 6 Emperor's Divide gives you a knock-up escape/peel tool that finally punishes his all-in attempts, and by level 6 your roam threat with soldier walls starts to outweigh his single-target poke.","late":"With Nashor's and Rabadon's online your wave clear and soldier range eclipse his kit, and in teamfights Emperor's Divide splits his team before Pyroclasm can chain — full-build Azir has more range and more sustained damage than a mage with no mobility.","whys":["Brand's passive burn plus Sear stun threatens kill windows before you have any items to trade back","Continued poke chips your HP every wave while your own damage still lags behind his combo","Brand keeps abusing cooldowns on cannon waves to zone you from CS and prevent safe soldier extensions","Soldier DPS catches up here — his combo still kills, but only if Sear connects first","Your level 6 Emperor's Divide creates disengage/peel that neutralizes his kill pressure, tipping the lane","Nashor's turns soldier poke into shred, and your wave clear and range finally outpace his burst","Fully scaled Azir with Divide and soldier walls dominates teamfights that a mage with no escape can't survive"]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"cassiopeia","win":["Cassiopeia","Cassiopeia","Skill","Skill","Cassiopeia","Cassiopeia","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Miasma is the grounding field, not her Q — inside it your Shifting Sands dash is disabled and she free-stacks Noxious Blast onto you."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Petrifying Gaze stuns only enemies facing her, and its 825-range cone sets up a Twin Fang burst that fires every 0.75 seconds."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Rabadon's pushes her poison DPS past your soldier poke, and Miasma still clears waves and fences you off the ground you want."},{"when":"Late","text":"At full build Emperor's Divide is the answer: Cassiopeia has no dash, so a wall behind her cuts her off from her team and the soldiers do the rest."}],"wants":{"you":["Play at max soldier range and never dash through her Miasma zones","Trade when Miasma is down — grounded, your E cannot get you out","Group early for objectives since 1v1 scaling favors her almost the whole game"],"foe":["Lay Miasma on the wave to zone you off CS and poison you passively","Land Petrifying Gaze to guarantee a Twin Fang follow-up","Kite in her poison cloud where your dashes get grounded and punished"]},"early":"Cassiopeia's Miasma denies you safe farming spots and grounds your Shifting Sands dash, while Twin Fang deals bonus damage to poisoned targets and heals her for part of it — you're forced into a soldier-poke lane where her chip pays her back. Track Miasma is 24s at rank 1, 16s at rank 5, and it grounds — your E will not fire inside it. Check the cloud before every step-up.","mid":"Petrifying Gaze stuns everyone facing her, and paired with a 0.75-second Twin Fang it is a burst combo you survive only by turning away or walling her — so this stays her lane through the mid game.","late":"It isn't until Emperor's Divide and a second item that you can wall off her Petrifying Gaze setup or knock her out of her own poison — full-build Azir out-ranges her, and because Cassiopeia has no dash a wall behind her ends the skirmish she started before Twin Fang heals her back.","whys":["Noxious Blast reaches 850 on a 3.5s cooldown against your 525 soldier — she pokes at level 1 and you cannot answer","Her poison stacking and Twin Fang scaling punish every trade attempt you make","Continued zoning keeps you starved for CS while she snowballs her passive damage","Twin Fang fires every 0.75s and heals her, so she wins any trade that lasts past your poke","Petrifying Gaze stuns anyone facing her and hands Twin Fang a free burst window","Even with your first item her poison DPS and wave clear still edge out your soldier damage","Full-build Emperor's Divide finally gives you the tools to interrupt her combo and win late skirmishes"]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"diana","win":["Diana","Diana","Skill","Diana","Skill","Diana","Azir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Crescent Strike marks you and Lunar Rush becomes free, so she arrives with Pale Cascade's shield already up and three spheres left to detonate."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Moonfall pulls from 475 and slows, forcing an all-in the moment Crescent Strike lands — and the marked dash means she never has to walk to you."},{"when":"1st item","text":"She keeps the all-in edge on her first item, punishing any Azir who spends Shifting Sands on poke instead of saving it for her jump."},{"when":"Late","text":"Emperor's Divide plus full soldier walls finally let you zone her jump-ins and win the fight before she closes the gap."}],"wants":{"you":["Hold soldiers in a defensive triangle so her dash-ins get walled instead of landing free","Track Crescent Strike cooldown before extending for CS near the sidebush","Play for scaling — group mid game since she wants isolated 1v1 pressure"],"foe":["Land Crescent Strike to enable a guaranteed jump with Pale Cascade shield up","Use Moonfall to pull you in range of a burst combo right after 6","Look to reset all-ins off jungle ganks since her kit rewards aggressive dives"]},"early":"Crescent Strike marks you with Moonlight and that makes Lunar Rush free, so the arc landing is the dive starting. Pale Cascade's spheres detonate in melee range, so she punishes any wave you shove too far forward. Track Crescent Strike is 8s at rank 1, 6s at rank 5, and it applies Moonlight — while you are marked, Lunar Rush has NO cooldown. Sidestep the arc and her dash is back on 22s at rank 1.","mid":"Her all-in only gets scarier at 6 with Moonfall's pull, letting her force fights the instant Crescent Strike is up — this is her most dangerous window and you need Divide or ally peel to survive it, though there are stretches where her cooldowns are down and trades even out.","late":"With Emperor's Divide unlocked and a full soldier wall up, you finally have the tools to zone her jump-in entirely, forcing her to walk into your Divide knockup before she can ever close the gap — full-build Azir out-ranges and out-scales a diving assassin-bruiser.","whys":["Crescent Strike reaches 900 to your 525 soldier and farms the wave as it pokes — level 1 she chips you for free","Her Pale Cascade shield-and-burst combo keeps punishing any close-range poke exchange","Both sides trade evenly here as her cooldowns cycle and your soldier positioning offsets her jump","A landed Crescent Strike refunds Lunar Rush, so one arc buys her two dashes onto you","Emperor's Divide walls Lunar Rush outright, so her only gap-closer stops working on your terms","She still finds pick windows off jungle assists or isolated roams at this phase","Full Emperor's Divide plus scaled soldiers finally let you wall her dash and win the extended fight"]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"ekko","win":["Ekko","Ekko","Skill","Ekko","Skill","Ekko","Azir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Ekko's Timewinder-into-Parallel Convergence combo threatens a slow-then-stun through your soldier zone if you're caught pushing."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Chronobreak rewind lets him all-in freely since any bad trade can be undone, making his level 6 dive extremely low-risk."},{"when":"1st item","text":"His first-item burst still edges your poke, and Phase Dive's reset means he arrives, kills and blinks out before your soldiers cycle."},{"when":"Late","text":"Emperor's Divide interrupts his Convergence zone setup, giving you the disengage to survive his all-in and win with full-build range."}],"wants":{"you":["Watch for his W field expanding — don't stand still in it or you eat a slow plus stun","Deny his roams by pushing waves fast so he can't reset for a side-lane gank","Save Divide specifically to knock him out of a completed Parallel Convergence zone"],"foe":["Set up Parallel Convergence early then walk you into the stun for a burst combo","Use Chronobreak to take risk-free all-ins since a bad trade rewinds","Roam off Timewinder slows to snowball sidelanes since Azir has weak 1v9 map presence early"]},"early":"Ekko's Parallel Convergence zone stuns anyone who lingers inside it, and Timewinder's slow lets him set that trap up even through your soldier poke — because Chronobreak makes his all-ins reversible, he can afford to take risks in lane that you can't. Track Chronobreak is 110s at rank 1 and only 50s at rank 3, and it heals him — hold Grievous Wounds and your final damage for after the rewind.","mid":"He remains ahead through level 6 since Chronobreak-backed dives are low-risk and his roams punish your lack of early map presence, though there are windows where his cooldowns are down and trades are closer to even; only once you hit Emperor's Divide can you reliably interrupt his zone setup and turn a fight back in your favor.","late":"With Divide online you can finally knock him out of a completed Convergence field before the stun lands, and full soldier scaling plus item power lets you out-damage him in extended fights — a scaled Azir has more sustained pressure than an assassin whose combo you can now disrupt.","whys":["Level 1 is his: Timewinder slows and hits twice from 1075 while one soldier is all you have — farm through it and spend no mana on poke","Level 2 is his: Timewinder hits going out and coming back from 1075 and Phase Dive closes 325 onto a soldier trade — two soldiers do not out-trade that yet.","Both sides find even trades here as cooldowns cycle and neither combo is guaranteed to land","Phase Dive blinks every 8s with an auto reset, so he picks every trade you take","Emperor's Divide gives you the interrupt tool to knock him out of a completed Convergence field","He can still punish you if he's snowballed a side lane and out-items you at this point","Full-build Azir range and soldier scaling overwhelm an assassin whose all-in you can now counter"]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"fizz","win":["Fizz","Fizz","Fizz","Fizz","Skill","Skill","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Fizz's Playful/Trickster untargetability lets him dodge your soldier volleys entirely while landing Seastone Trident poke for free."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Chum the Waters fish lands a slow-then-burst combo, and his untargetable hop makes him nearly impossible to punish on the way in."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your soldier wall and Conquering Sands wave clear finally start out-ranging his short-hop poke pattern once Nashor's is done."},{"when":"Late","text":"Emperor's Divide and full soldiers let you zone his jump entirely — a scaled Azir out-ranges Fizz's short all-in kit completely."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait Playful/Trickster before committing soldiers so it whiffs on nothing","Hold max range and let him waste E poke into your minions instead of you","Scale toward Divide/Liandry's — this matchup flips hard once you have items"],"foe":["Poke with Trident procs and E while untargetable during Playful/Trickster","Land Chum the Waters for a slow into a full burst all-in near level 6","Force short trades he can escape from instantly with his hop, denying your soldier retaliation"]},"early":"Fizz's Playful/Trickster hop makes him untouchable to soldier autos while he pokes freely with Seastone Trident procs, and Chum the Waters near level 6 turns any hit into a slow-locked burst combo you can't easily escape — respect his range and never overextend soldiers into poke range. Track Playful/Trickster is 16s at rank 1 and 8s at rank 5, and it dodges your volley AND grounds you — your E does not fire while it is on you.","mid":"By level 6 your kit catches up: Conquering Sands clears the wave, your soldiers out-range his 400-range hop, and Emperor's Divide punishes the commit — once Playful/Trickster is spent you get 8 to 16 seconds to hit him from max range.","late":"With Emperor's Divide and full item scaling, your soldier zone control simply out-ranges Fizz's short-hop kit — he has no way to close distance safely once you can knock him back the instant he commits, making late-game Azir heavily favored.","whys":["Urchin Strike is a 550-range dash through your soldier and Nimble Fighter walks him through minions — level 1 he reaches you and you cannot push him off","Seastone Trident empowers his autos and Urchin Strike is 8s — two soldiers do not out-trade the dash-in, so hold the poke","Playful/Trickster lands at 3: he hops over your Q and lands on top of you, and Shifting Sands is 22s to his 16s — two entries for every escape","Seastone Trident is 5s by rank 3 and resets his auto, and Playful/Trickster is still up for every trade he starts — inside 550 he out-chips you and leaves.","Emperor's Divide walls his dash and answers Chum the Waters the moment the shark commits","Item power and cooldown reduction let you punish his commitments before he can escape","Full-build Divide and soldier walls completely zone out his short-range all-in kit"]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"galio","win":["Galio","Galio","Galio","Galio","Galio","Azir","Azir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Winds of War is a damage-over-time tornado at 825, and Justice Punch's 650 dash knocks you clean off any soldier setup you just built."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Hero's Entrance ultimate lets him roam and reset lane state instantly, punishing any prio you built up before he teleports back in."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your Conquering Sands wave clear starts matching his poke, but he still holds more raw utility and safety than you at this point."},{"when":"Late","text":"Emperor's Divide and full soldier scaling finally let you out-damage his tanky poke kit and punish his cooldown windows in skirmishes."}],"wants":{"you":["Farm from behind soldiers and avoid clumping near Winds of War's slow zone","Track his ultimate roam timing so you're not caught overextended when he teleports away","Scale patiently — this matchup swings hard once you have Divide and full items"],"foe":["Zone with the Winds of War tornado to deny your CS and soldier setup","Use Justice Punch to interrupt your combos and knock you out of position","Roam globally with Hero's Entrance to swing sidelanes while you can't punish the absence"]},"early":"Winds of War is a damage-over-time tornado at 825 that denies your soldier positioning, and Justice Punch's 650 knockback disrupts any wave you try to set up, while his tanky base stats mean early trades rarely favor you — and Shield of Durand's taunt makes any step inside 275 a full combo. Track Justice Punch is 11s at rank 1 and 7s at rank 5 — the 650 dash knocks up the first champion it hits, so step up only on its downtime.","mid":"Hero's Entrance lets him fly globally to swing other lanes and land back before you can capitalize, keeping him ahead through the roam-heavy midgame, though your wave clear with Conquering Sands starts closing the gap as you approach your first real item spike.","late":"Once Emperor's Divide comes online alongside full soldier scaling, your damage output and zone control finally outpace his tanky poke-and-utility kit — a scaled Azir punishes his cooldown windows and out-ranges his engage tools in teamfights.","whys":["Winds of War is a tornado that burns over time from 825 and out-ranges your sand","Continued zoning and safe trades keep you starved for value in this stretch","Justice Punch knocks up the first champion it reaches, and it returns every 11 seconds","Roam pressure and lane state resets keep the phase in his favor through midgame","Hero's Entrance is global — he swings a sidelane and lands back before your crash pays","Item power lets you begin trading evenly, though he still holds a slight utility edge","Full-build Divide and soldier scaling let you out-damage and out-zone his tanky kit late"]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"hwei","win":["Hwei","Hwei","Hwei","Hwei","Hwei","Azir","Azir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Hwei's Devastating Fire and Severing Bolt chunk you from max range while your soldier volleys whiff on his spacing — expect to be pushed off farm repeatedly."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"His ultimate combos threaten a full burst if you're caught pushed up, but your R (Emperor's Divide) starts giving you a real disengage option to survive dives."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Soldier waveclear and safer long-range poke finally let you match his zoning instead of just absorbing it — you stop losing the lane outright."},{"when":"Late","text":"Your R + soldier wall control zones teamfights harder than his single-target combos, and you out-scale his damage ceiling with full build."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive lane without losing more than a few hundred gold","Hit 6 with mana for E-shield escapes","Reach 1st item to start trading poke for poke"],"foe":["Snowball poke leads into a kill before 6","Zone you off farm to stunt your scaling","Land ult combos to burst you in one rotation"]},"early":"Hwei's Q variants let him poke you from beyond your Q range while denying your soldier placement with Devastating Fire zoning. You cannot contest CS trades directly — W-farming from max range is safer than walking up. Play around minion waves for cover and hold E for emergencies since one bad engage from him can chunk half your health. Ban-worthy if you're not confident soaking poke.","mid":"Once you hit 6 you gain E-to-soldier mobility and R as a disengage/peel tool, which softens his all-in threat, but he still out-ranges your poke pre-item. Play for wave control and roams rather than direct trades — Hwei has no dash, so if you can get vision and flank with jungle/support you can punish his positioning. Continue prioritizing CS over trades until your first back.","late":"With Nashor's Tooth and Rabadon's online your soldiers finally out-range and out-damage his combo pieces, and your R wall shuts his engage options down completely. Build MR (Abyssal Mask or Banshee's) if he's ahead, since his Signature burst stays lethal if he catches you without a shield up. In teamfights, zone with soldiers from max range and only R when he commits — his single-target burst can't answer your area control once you're ahead on items.","whys":["Level 1: Subject: Disaster gives him three damaging paints from level 1, and every one of them out-ranges your soldier.","Level 2: He adds a second poke tool, compounding chip damage you can't answer without soldiers up.","Level 3: His full poke kit is online and safely zones your farm from outside your threat range.","Levels 4-5: The gap is at its worst — his paints return every 6-10s while Conquering Sands is still 12s or more and your E is 22s.","Level 6: Your R finally gives you a disengage tool, narrowing the gap even though his ult combo can still burst you.","First item: Your poke and clear catch up enough that you're no longer strictly losing the exchange.","2+ items: Your zone control and scaling damage overtake his combo ceiling, flipping the matchup in your favor."]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"irelia","win":["Irelia","Skill","Skill","Irelia","Azir","Azir","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Bladesurge resets off every Marked target for 15 mana, so she chains dashes to close on you before your soldier volley cycles — she can force an all-in straight through your zone."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Azir's Shurima's Legacy area denial plus Emperor's Divide wall now lets you body-block her dash-ins and cut her escape after she commits."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Both spike on completed first items, but Azir's range and wave-clear scale better from here, letting you punish her for walking up."},{"when":"Late","text":"Full items you out-range and out-poke her completely — she has to flank through a side lane instead of walking down mid."}],"wants":{"you":["Hold soldiers passively and only trade when she's used Bladesurge on a minion","Freeze the wave near your tower levels 1-5 to deny her dash targets","Ult to wall off her engage and disengage the instant she commits"],"foe":["Farm with Bladesurge off minions to poke you for free and reset the cooldown","All-in the instant you overextend or your soldiers are on cooldown","Dive with the jungler once Vanguard's Edge can wall off your escape route"]},"early":"Irelia's Bladesurge lets her dash minion-to-you for free trades while resetting off anything Marked, and Ionian Fervor stacks her attack speed fast, so keep soldiers between you and any minion she could jump off — deny the dash angle and only push when Bladesurge is down. Track Flawless Duet is 16s at rank 1, 10s at rank 5. It stuns, Marks AND grounds — grounded, your E will not fire, and the Mark refreshes her Bladesurge. Dodge the converge and the dive dies.","mid":"By level 6 your Shurima's Legacy zone and Emperor's Divide wall give you real tools to punish her engage: wall between her and you the moment she Bladesurges in, or use the terrain to cut off her follow-up dash entirely, turning her all-in into a bad trade.","late":"With a full build your range advantage and wave-clear let you sit back and shove into her face without ever entering dash range, forcing her to look for side-lane splits or flanks instead of a straight mid duel — this is where the matchup fully turns in your favor.","whys":["Irelia's Bladesurge resets off minions for 15 mana, giving her free poke and stacking attack speed you cannot answer","Same dash-reset pressure continues to snowball if you overextend near minions","She's still ahead on stats and all-in potential before your kit comes online","Levels 4-5 stay hers: Flawless Duet stuns between the blades on 16s, and a Bladesurge that lands with the stun brings the full Ionian Fervor stack onto you before Shifting Sands is back.","Your ultimate wall and zone finally give you tools to shut down her engage","Your item power and wave-clear pull you clearly ahead here","Fully scaled Azir out-ranges and out-waveclears her, forcing her off mid entirely"]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"karma","win":["Karma","Karma","Karma","Karma","Skill","Azir","Azir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Karma's cheap mana costs and Soul-Flare-empowered Q let her chip you from range every wave while you're still fragile without your soldiers fully up."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Emperor's Divide gives you the first real engage/disengage tool of the game, and her Mantra mostly buys shields and roams rather than raw damage."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Once you finish a burst item you one-shot with E-Q-AA combos through soldiers, while her damage plateaus without a first item-tier scaling."},{"when":"Late","text":"Full build you completely outrange and outscale her poke, forcing her into a pure support/roam role rather than a lane threat."}],"wants":{"you":["Play passive and farm behind soldiers, avoid walking up into her Q range","Ping and track her roams — Karma's shields exist to enable others, so watch top/bot","Look to all-in the instant you hit 6 and she's spent RQ/RW recently"],"foe":["Poke you down every wave with mana-efficient Q while staying safe","Roam early with Mantra-Tether to swing sidelanes since her own lane pressure fades late","Bait your all-in with a shield and punish the overextension"]},"early":"Karma's chip damage from Soul-Flare Q is nearly free on her mana bar, and she can poke you every time you go for a caster minion, so you need to stay behind your soldier wall and just absorb the early chip rather than trading back — this is a lane where you concede tempo and farm through it. Track Focused Resolve is a flat 12s at 675 range: break the tether with range or line of sight before it roots.","mid":"Once you hit level 6 the calculus flips: Emperor's Divide knocks her out of her own 675-range tether and punishes her for walking up to poke, and her Mantra is mostly spent on shields for roams rather than lane damage, so all-in when Inner Flame is down and her Inspire shield is on its 8-10 second cooldown.","late":"With items online your burst combo deletes her before her shield can save her, and your wave-clear and range dwarf anything she can do solo in lane, so a scaled Azir simply out-classes a scaled Karma one-on-one.","whys":["Her mana-efficient poke chips you for free while your kit is still clunky at low levels","The same poke pattern keeps compounding since she can spam Q far more than you can punish","Shifting Sands answers Focused Resolve, but Inner Flame is 9s to your 22s dash — she still edges the poke war","Karma's damage plateaus without strong scaling, and you're still slightly behind on raw poke","Your ultimate finally gives you the tools to punish her aggression and force all-ins","Item power lets your combo burst her down before her Mantra shield saves her","Full-build Azir out-ranges and out-damages a scaled Karma decisively"]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"kassadin","win":["Azir","Azir","Azir","Azir","Skill","Kassadin","Kassadin"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Kassadin is one of the weakest early laners in the game — his Q has a long cooldown and no shield yet, so your soldier zone poke wins every exchange for free."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Riftwalk gives him mobility but almost no burst this early, and your ult lets you wall him away from you or your soldiers entirely."},{"when":"1st item","text":"His first item plus Nether Blade's mana return lets him Riftwalk repeatedly — keep shoving, but stop stepping past your own sand."},{"when":"Late","text":"Riftwalk at 2 seconds and 40 mana chains blinks straight through your wall, so a full-build Kassadin beats you in a sidelane — fight only alongside your team."}],"wants":{"you":["Push every wave hard and deny his farm — he needs CS to function at all","Zone him off minions with soldiers so he can't sustain mana for Riftwalk spam","Roam constantly once ahead since he can't punish your absence early"],"foe":["Farm passively under tower and just survive to a scaling item spike","Avoid all trades until Riftwalk cooldown allows safe poke","Hope for jungle ganks to offset the lost CS and tempo"]},"early":"Kassadin is famously the weakest lane presence in the game before level 9 — his Q is short-range and long-cooldown, he has no defensive tool, and your soldier zone lets you poke him for free every single wave without any real answer from him. Track Riftwalk is 5s at rank 1, 3.5s at rank 2 and 2s at rank 3; repeat blinks cost extra mana, so punish the third one. His Q is 9s at rank 1, Force Pulse 21s.","mid":"Riftwalk at 6 gives him escape but negligible damage output this early, so you keep pressing your advantage: wall him off with your ult if he tries to engage, and keep shoving waves into his tower to starve his farm.","late":"Kassadin only has to survive to items: with Riftwalk at 2 seconds he re-enters every fight you thought you had won, so convert the early lead into towers and objectives instead of farming — a long game hands him the win condition soldiers cannot chase.","whys":["Your zone control and range punish his weak early kit with no real recourse for him","The same denial continues to snowball as he falls further behind on CS","He's still far behind in stats and tempo heading into his ult unlock","Levels 4-5 stay yours: Force Pulse needs six spells cast near him to charge, and your soldier summons count — so cast W behind the wave, not on top of him, and drag Qs through him on every last-hit.","Your ultimate lets you wall his limited engage tools away entirely","His first item plus a 3.5s Riftwalk turns escape into kills","Two items in, Riftwalk is a 3.5s blink he can stack, and Nether Blade's reset finishes what the blink starts — Emperor's Divide answers one entry, and he has three more before it returns."]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"katarina","win":["Skill","Katarina","Katarina","Katarina","Katarina","Azir","Azir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Bouncing Blade costs nothing on an 11-second cooldown and Voracity refunds her cooldowns off any kill near her, so one pick around your soldiers snowballs the lane."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Her ult is a global execute threat on low-health targets across the map, so she can punish your roams even when she's not in lane."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Once you finish your burst item you can delete her before she gets her dagger reset off, flipping the all-in math in your favor."},{"when":"Late","text":"Full items your range and zone keep her out entirely — she has to flank from a side lane instead of dueling you mid."}],"wants":{"you":["Keep soldiers spread to deny easy dagger-reset angles off you","Play safe around low HP minions and wards since her ult snowballs off any kill","Punish her when Shunpo is on cooldown — that's her only true engage/escape"],"foe":["Farm safely and look for dagger-reset all-ins the instant you misposition","Ult to snowball kills across the map once she's ahead","Bait you into overextending near low-HP minions for a free Death Lotus reset"]},"early":"Katarina's daggers reset off kills near your soldiers, and if she catches you low or overextended her all-in can snowball out of control fast, so you want to keep your distance, avoid clumping low-health minions near you, and only trade when Shunpo is clearly down. Track Shunpo is 12s at rank 1 falling to 8s, 725 range, and free — it is her entry and her exit, so step up only once she spends it. Death Lotus is 75s at rank 1 and it is a channel: Emperor's Divide knocks her out of it.","mid":"Her ultimate is a 550-range channel rather than a global threat, so it only hurts if she is already standing on you — hold Emperor's Divide for the moment she starts spinning, and keep your HP high enough that Voracity never gets the kill that refunds her kit.","late":"Once you finish a burst item, your E-Q combo can delete her outright before she gets a reset off, and your range keeps her at arm's length — a scaled Azir simply out-trades and out-positions her in a straight lane fight.","whys":["Neither side has a clear tool edge yet at level 1-2, it's an even skill matchup","Her dagger-reset snowball potential starts to threaten you if you misplay","The reset threat compounds and her all-in becomes scarier the longer it goes unchecked","Her ability to snowball off any kill anywhere keeps her ahead through this stretch","Level 6 is hers: Death Lotus is a 75s channel at 550 range and Emperor's Divide is 120s — you get one wall for every two of her ults, so the level 6 all-in is hers until you land it.","Your burst item lets you kill her before she gets a Death Lotus reset off","Full-build Azir's range and zone control keep a scaled Katarina locked out of lane"]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"leblanc","win":["LeBlanc","LeBlanc","LeBlanc","LeBlanc","Skill","Skill","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"LeBlanc's Sigil burst plus Distortion dash-in-dash-out can chunk or kill you before your soldiers even land — she trades on her terms entirely."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Her ult adds a second burst window, but your R now gives you a wall to block her dash engage or cut off her return path."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Mana and AP let your poke and clear match her burst threat, and your soldiers start punishing her cooldown windows after she commits Distortion."},{"when":"Late","text":"Your zone control and R punish her all-in windows hard — she has no way to burst through a full-build Azir who can just wall her off."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive her burst windows without dying pre-6","Track her Distortion cooldown to know when it's safe to push","Reach 1st item so poke damage starts threatening her back"],"foe":["Land a full burst combo through Sigil+Distortion+Q for a kill","Snowball a solo kill into permanent lane control","Avoid overextending once your R wall is online"]},"early":"LeBlanc can one-shot-adjacent you with Sigil of Malice into Distortion in and out before you can react, especially with no minions to soldier-block. Never let her walk up freely with Distortion up — that's her all-in window. Ward the river/tri-bush if possible and play passively, prioritizing not dying over contesting CS. Her only weakness is Distortion's long cooldown, so track it.","mid":"After 6, Mimic gives her a second cast of a basic spell on a 45-second cooldown, so the burst can arrive twice — but Emperor's Divide knocks her back out of the 600-range dash she opens with. Keep playing safe and let soldiers chip; avoid pushing the wave into her range where she can burst you clean. Group with your jungler for skirmishes rather than dueling her 1v1 pre-item.","late":"Once you have your first mage item your poke and wave clear catch up to her burst threat, and by two items your R and soldier zone control simply outclass her single burst combo — if she doesn't kill you in one rotation, she has nothing else. Build a defensive item (Zhonya's or Banshee's) if she's fed, since her burst still one-shots squishies even late. In fights, keep soldiers spread to threaten her flank routes and use R to wall her off from your backline.","whys":["Level 1: LeBlanc's Sigil poke already threatens more damage than your uncharged soldier summon can trade back.","Level 2: Distortion comes online, letting her all-in and retreat safely before you can punish.","Level 3: Her full burst combo is live and can kill you outright if you're caught without minions to block.","Levels 4-5: She reaches peak burst-to-cooldown ratio dominance while you remain immobile and reactive.","Level 6: Your R gives you your first real tool to block her engage, narrowing but not closing the gap against her ult-enabled double burst.","First item: Your poke and clear catch up enough to start contesting her cooldown windows instead of just surviving them.","2+ items: Your zone control and wall completely neutralize her all-in, and she has no scaling answer to your late-game dominance."]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"lissandra","win":["Skill","Azir","Lissandra","Lissandra","Lissandra","Azir","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Lissandra needs to land Ice Shard/claw combos to threaten you, and your soldier spacing actually holds up decently here — but she catches up once she has combo rhythm down."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Her ult-enabled all-in (Glacial Path reset into R stun) turns lane fully in her favor since you have no reliable way to avoid a point-blank stun-lock before your own R is up."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Mana and poke damage let you punish her Glacial Path windows hard — Ice Shard reaches 725, and your soldier line reaches 740."},{"when":"Late","text":"Your R wall shuts down her one-dimensional dive-and-stun engage completely, and your zone control outscales her single burst combo threat."}],"wants":{"you":["Punish her when Glacial Path is on cooldown","Survive her level 6 all-in window","Snowball poke damage into a 1st-item lead"],"foe":["Land Glacial Path resets to stick to you","Force a level 6 all-in kill before you can react","Deny your soldier zoning with dive pressure"]},"early":"Ice Shard reaches 725 but Ring of Frost only 450, so if you keep soldiers up and hold the space between those two numbers you win most early trades — she has to walk in to do real damage. Watch for jungle ganks, since Ring of Frost roots you flat for the follow-up. Keep your spacing disciplined and you out-farm her cleanly here.","mid":"The moment she hits 6, her Glacial Path-reset-into-R combo becomes a real kill threat, since her ultimate stun is nearly unavoidable at close range and you have no answer until your own R comes online. Play very cautious around her level 6 spike — don't overextend even if you were winning lane before. Once you're past that window and hit your own 6, your R gives you a way to wall off her dive path or peel yourself from her engage.","late":"With your first mage item your poke starts to comfortably outdamage anything she can do outside of landing a full combo, and by two items your R and soldier walls completely nullify her engage-reliant kit — she has no way to reach you safely. Build MR if she's fed off picks (Abyssal Mask), and always hold R in fights to block her dive onto your backline. She has almost no scaling beyond her burst combo, so a full-build Azir simply overwhelms her with zone control.","whys":["Level 1: Ice Shard reaches 725 but your soldier line reaches 740, so spacing wins the level-1 trade.","Level 2: She still lacks the tools to punish your zoning, keeping the early trade advantage in your favor.","Level 3: Her combo rhythm (Ice Shard into claw) starts landing more consistently, closing the early gap.","Levels 4-5: She's fully capable of punishing any misstep with a full combo, flipping small advantages her way.","Level 6: Her ultimate turns her into a near-unavoidable all-in threat that you have no answer to until your own R is online.","First item: Your poke damage starts punishing her long cooldowns hard since she has no answer at range.","2+ items: Your R and zone control shut down her one-note dive engage completely, ending her relevance in the matchup."]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"locke","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Locke","Skill","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Locke's early kit lets him pressure your lane before your soldiers reach full uptime, so he can force trades you aren't equipped to answer yet."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"His ultimate adds a fresh layer of engage or burst to any all-in, keeping this window dangerous even once your kit is online."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Both sides trade evenly once itemized — whoever plays the wave and cooldowns better wins the exchange from here."},{"when":"Late","text":"With full builds this comes down to positioning and target prioritization in fights rather than a clear kit advantage either way."}],"wants":{"you":["Play patient behind soldiers early and avoid unnecessary trades","Track his cooldowns before committing to any extended trade","Use your zone control to contest neutral objectives once scaled"],"foe":["Pressure the lane early while his kit is ahead of yours","Look for all-in windows around his ultimate's availability","Play for even skirmishes once both sides reach core items"]},"early":"Locke's kit gives him the edge in the first trades of the lane, so you want to play patient, farm behind your soldiers, and avoid extending trades until you have more tools online. Track Locke Ritual Nails (Marks): matchup-defining — The nail marks are his whole engine — without 2-3 stacks on you his blink-in barely dents; sidestep the recasts and punish the ten seconds of nothing. Track it before every step-up.","mid":"His ultimate keeps him a threat through level 6, and the fight stays close to even as both kits come online around your first item spikes — this is a skill-dependent stretch where wave management and cooldown tracking decide who wins each exchange.","late":"By the late game neither champion has a clean kit advantage over the other — outcomes here come down to positioning, itemization choices, and execution rather than raw power differences.","whys":["Locke's early kit lets him win the first trades before your soldiers are fully online","He keeps pressing that same early advantage through this stretch","This window is even and comes down to who plays their cooldowns and wave better","Both kits are online and trading fairly evenly here","His ultimate keeps him ahead in raw all-in potential at this level","This is an even, skill-dependent stretch with no clear kit edge either way","Late game outcomes here hinge on execution rather than a structural advantage"]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"lux","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Azir","Azir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Light Binding at 1175 into Lucent Singularity at 1100 outranges everything you own — your Q reaches 740, so she chips you for free."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Her ult adds a huge burst finisher to any landed root, but your own R lets you start threatening disengage or counter-zoning."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your poke and clear finally match her range, and soldiers start punishing her positioning when she pokes from max range."},{"when":"Late","text":"Your zone control and R wall dominate her single-target poke pattern, and you out-scale her damage ceiling comfortably with items."}],"wants":{"you":["Avoid getting rooted into a follow-up combo","Survive to 1st item without losing lane outright","Punish her when Light Binding is on cooldown"],"foe":["Land Light Binding to set up burst or a kill","Zone you off farm with safe long-range poke","Snowball a root-into-ult kill before you scale"]},"early":"Lux's binding range and poke damage outclass your kit before your soldiers are fully online, so she can chip you at will while punishing any careless soldier placement with a root. Play behind minions, don't waste Q on empty pushes, and watch for jungle ganks that pair with her root for an easy kill. Farming under tower with W is safer than contesting trades directly.","mid":"At 6 her ult massively raises the threat of any landed root into a burst combo, so respect her poke even more in this window — but your own R gives you a way to wall off engages or create separation in skirmishes. Look for opportunities to punish her when Light Binding is down, since she has no other engage tool. Group for roams rather than forcing lane trades in this stretch.","late":"Once you have your first item your poke range and clear start to match hers, letting you contest trades instead of just surviving them, and by two items your zone control with soldiers plus R completely overwhelms her single-target poke pattern. Build MR (Abyssal Mask) if she's ahead, since her burst combo remains dangerous even late. In teamfights, spread soldiers to bait her root and only commit R once she's used Light Binding.","whys":["Level 1: Lux's binding range already outreaches your uncharged Q, letting her poke you safely from range.","Level 2: She adds more consistent poke pressure while you remain cooldown-limited and immobile.","Level 3: Her full poke kit is online and continues to zone you off farm from outside your effective range.","Levels 4-5: The disparity peaks as she can freely poke and punish any overextension with a root-into-follow-up.","Level 6: Her ultimate massively raises the stakes of any landed root, though your own R starts giving you counterplay.","First item: Your poke and clear finally reach parity, letting you start trading back instead of just absorbing damage.","2+ items: Your zone control and wall completely dominate her single-target poke pattern, flipping the matchup decisively."]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"malzahar","win":["Malzahar","Malzahar","Malzahar","Malzahar","Malzahar","Azir","Azir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Malzahar's Void Swarm/Malefic Visions poke and passive shield let him win extended trades while you're still cooldown-starved and immobile."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Nether Grasp is a suppression, not a root — 700 range on 140 seconds, and nothing you own escapes it until your own R can break the channel."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your poke and clear catch up and your R gives you a way to break line of sight or wall off his ultimate's follow-up before he can land the full combo."},{"when":"Late","text":"Your zone control and superior scaling outclass his DoT-based damage profile, and R lets you disengage from his suppress entirely if you play around vision."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive his DoT poke and passive-shield trades pre-6","Avoid being isolated for a suppress-ult kill","Reach 1st item to start out-ranging his poke"],"foe":["Stack Malefic Visions damage to win the sustained trade","Land Malefic Visions, then follow with the suppress before you scale","Isolate you with vision control for a guaranteed suppress kill"]},"early":"Void Shift gives him damage reduction and crowd-control immunity whenever he has not just been hit, so a soldier auto to strip it comes before any trade, and his DoT wins prolonged exchanges against your cooldown-heavy kit. Nether Grasp is a near-guaranteed kill if you are caught alone without vision, so respect river bushes and track his position. This is one of the more dangerous pre-6 matchups you get — play it passively.","mid":"Once you hit 6 your R finally gives you an option to break line of sight or wall off his engage path, softening the suppress-kill threat, though he remains capable of winning sustained trades with his DoT and shield. Prioritize vision control around river and jungle entrances to avoid getting isolated. Look to out-rotate him with soldier zone pressure on side waves rather than committing to lane duels.","late":"Your first item lets your poke and clear start matching his sustained damage, and by two items your zone control and R clearly outscale his single-combo suppress threat — as long as you stay warded, his kill window shrinks dramatically. Build a QSS or similar if his suppress is repeatedly deciding fights, since it remains his one high-impact tool throughout the game. In teamfights, keep soldiers spread and never walk into fog without vision, since his ultimate ignores most defensive tools besides removal.","whys":["Level 1: Void Shift gives him damage reduction and CC immunity until a soldier auto strips it off him.","Level 2: His Void Swarm adds more consistent poke, further tilting extended exchanges in his favor.","Level 3: His full poke and sustain combo is online, continuing to outlast your limited early trading tools.","Levels 4-5: The gap peaks as his DoT stacking wins any prolonged fight you're forced into.","Level 6: His suppress ultimate is a near-guaranteed kill against your zero-mobility kit before your own R comes online.","First item: Your poke and clear catch up enough to stop losing sustained trades outright.","2+ items: Your zone control and disengage options outscale his DoT damage profile, flipping the matchup with proper vision play."]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"mel","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Azir","Azir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Mel's 950-range Radiant Volley and Rebuttal's damage immunity punish careless soldier trades, chipping you down faster than your cooldown-limited tools answer."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Her ultimate adds burst-execute pressure to any poke lead she's built, but your own R comes online here to give you disengage and zone-control answers."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your poke damage and clear start to overpower her more one-dimensional ranged kit, and soldiers begin winning the wave-control war."},{"when":"Late","text":"Your superior zone control and scaling completely outclass her mid-game-focused kit, turning teamfights firmly in your favor with R plus soldiers."}],"wants":{"you":["Avoid feeding her passive reflect damage in early trades","Survive to 6 without falling too far behind on CS","Reach 1st item to flip poke damage in your favor"],"foe":["Poke you down consistently before you scale","Snowball a lead into a lvl 6 execute kill","Deny your farm and zone control before your items come online"]},"early":"Rebuttal, not her passive, is the reflect — it prevents her taking damage for its duration, so never poke into it and farm with soldiers from max range. Her passive stacks Overwhelm on everything that hits you, and free chip now becomes Golden Eclipse damage at 6. Radiant Volley is a 10-second cooldown at rank 1; don't overextend for CS while it is up.","mid":"At 6 her ultimate threatens to execute you if she's built a damage lead, but this is also when your own R comes online, giving you a real tool to disengage or wall off her line of sight. Play for wave management and side-lane pressure with soldiers rather than direct duels in this stretch. If you can avoid dying to her level 6 spike, your scaling starts to take over quickly after.","late":"Your first item brings your poke and clear to a level that starts overwhelming her more limited kit, and by two items your zone control with R and soldiers is simply superior to anything she brings to a teamfight. Build MR if she's ahead on kills (Abyssal Mask), since her burst execute remains a threat into squishies. In fights, use soldiers to control space and hold R to block her engage or peel for your team.","whys":["Level 1: Mel's ranged poke and reflect passive already win trades against your cooldown-limited early kit.","Level 2: She continues to out-poke you consistently while you lack answers at this range.","Level 3: Her full trading pattern is online, continuing to chip you down faster than you can respond.","Levels 4-5: The gap peaks as any careless trade feeds her reflect damage and compounds her lead.","Level 6: Her ultimate threatens an execute on any lead she's built, though your own R gives you your first real answer.","First item: Your poke and clear finally start to overpower her more one-dimensional kit.","2+ items: Your superior zone control and scaling completely take over the matchup in teamfights."]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"naafiri","win":["Naafiri","Naafiri","Naafiri","Naafiri","Naafiri","Naafiri","Azir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Naafiri's dash-heavy pack all-ins close the distance instantly and shred you before your soldiers can even land — this window is brutal for you."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Her ult lets her leap onto you from absurd range with pack support, and even your own R can struggle to fully stop a coordinated dive here."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Nashor's lets you punish the 11-second Eviscerate gap with soldier poke, though she is still lethal the moment she catches you off a minion."},{"when":"Late","text":"Your zone control and R wall finally give you the tools to keep her out entirely — she has almost no way to close the gap against a full-build Azir who plays safe."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive her all-in windows without feeding a snowball","Hold R for her dash-in engage rather than wasting it early","Reach 1st item to start answering her dive pattern with poke"],"foe":["Chain dashes through minions to close the gap and kill you","Snowball an early kill into permanent lane dominance","Catch you out of position for her ultimate leap"]},"early":"Naafiri simply closes distance faster than you can create space, and her passive pack of doggos adds extra damage to any all-in — this is one of your hardest lanes pre-6. Play maximally passive, keep minions between you and her, and don't push the wave since a pushed lane invites a free dash-in kill. Ask jungle for early attention if she starts snowballing.","mid":"Her ultimate adds a long-range leap to her all-in kit, letting her close gaps you thought were safe, so respect her all-in potential even at 6 when your own R comes online. Use R defensively to wall off her dash path rather than trying to trade — you're still the weaker combatant in a direct fight here. Focus on farming safely and avoid dying, since your scaling is what wins this matchup, not early trades.","late":"Once you have your first item you can start punishing her dash cooldowns with poke damage, though she remains a threat if she catches you isolated. By two items your zone control and R wall give you real answers to keep her out of range entirely, and your scaling damage output outclasses her flat snowball-reliant kit. Build early defensive stats (Zhonya's) if she's ahead, since a fed Naafiri can still delete you in one dash-chain. In fights, hold R until she commits her engage, then wall her off from your team.","whys":["Level 1: Darkin Daggers bleeds from 900 and her packmates leap onto whatever it hits, so she out-trades a single soldier.","Level 2: Her pack passive adds extra damage to any trade, further tilting close-range exchanges her way.","Level 3: Her full all-in combo is online and can kill you outright if you're caught without minions to block.","Levels 4-5: This is her peak dive window — she snowballs hard off any early kill while you remain immobile.","Level 6: Her ultimate adds a long-range leap to her engage, and even your own R struggles to fully answer a coordinated dive.","First item: Your poke starts punishing her dash cooldowns, though she remains dangerous if she catches you out of position.","2+ items: Your zone control and wall finally give you the tools to keep her out entirely, flipping the late-game in your favor."]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"neeko","win":["Neeko","Neeko","Neeko","Neeko","Neeko","Azir","Azir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Neeko's Blooming Burst and disguise-enabled ambushes punish your predictable soldier patterns, letting her poke and all-in you while you're still cooldown-heavy."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Her ultimate is a devastating teamfight/duel tool that can lock you down completely, though your own R now offers a way to wall off her engage."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your poke and clear start to match her burst-poke hybrid kit, and soldiers begin to win the wave-control battle back."},{"when":"Late","text":"Your zone control and superior scaling outclass her more burst-reliant kit, letting you dominate teamfights with R and soldier walls."}],"wants":{"you":["Play around her disguise to avoid ambush trades","Survive to 6 without falling behind on CS","Reach 1st item to start contesting her poke damage"],"foe":["Land Blooming Burst combos to poke or kill you pre-6","Use disguise to set up an unexpected all-in","Snowball her burst lead into permanent lane control"]},"early":"Neeko's burst poke and disguise trickery let her set up trades you won't see coming, punishing your immobile, cooldown-limited kit hard in this window. Be wary of jungle camps and minions that could be her in disguise, and avoid overextending since her burst combo can chunk you fast. Farm safely with W and don't contest her poke directly. Track Tangle-Barbs: 12s at rank 1, 10s at rank 5 — it roots everything it passes through, so minions do not block it; sidestep the line, never hide behind it.","mid":"Her ultimate is a powerful area-lock tool that can decide skirmishes and teamfights outright, so respect her all-in potential even after you hit 6, when your own R starts giving you a way to wall off her engage or peel. Focus on safe farming and side-wave pressure rather than direct duels in this stretch — her burst-heavy kit still edges you out in isolated fights. Look for opportunities to punish her when her key combo pieces are down.","late":"Once you have your first item your poke and clear finally start to match her burst-poke hybrid profile, and by two items your zone control with R and soldiers clearly outclasses her more burst-reliant kit in extended fights. Build MR (Abyssal Mask) if she's snowballed kills, since her burst combo remains a threat into squishies. In teamfights, spread soldiers to deny her ultimate's full value and hold R to block her engage.","whys":["Level 1: Neeko's burst poke already threatens more damage than your uncharged soldier trade can answer.","Level 2: Her disguise trickery adds ambush potential that further punishes your predictable early patterns.","Level 3: Her full poke-burst combo is online and continues to outtrade your cooldown-limited kit.","Levels 4-5: The gap peaks as her disguise and burst combo can punish any misstep severely.","Level 6: Her ultimate is a powerful lockdown tool, though your own R starts giving you a real answer to her engage.","First item: Your poke and clear finally catch up enough to contest her damage output directly.","2+ items: Your zone control and scaling outclass her more burst-reliant kit, flipping the late game in your favor."]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"orianna","win":["Orianna","Orianna","Orianna","Orianna","Orianna","Azir","Azir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Orianna's Command: Attack poke and ball-zoning punish your soldier placement, chipping you steadily while you lack the cooldowns to answer back."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Her ultimate is a game-deciding teamfight tool that can shockwave your whole team, but your own R now gives you disengage and wall-off options."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your poke and clear catch up to her ball-based zoning, letting soldiers start winning the wave-control fight back."},{"when":"Late","text":"Your superior scaling and zone control outclass her more team-oriented kit in extended fights, especially once you can wall off her Shockwave setup."}],"wants":{"you":["Play around her ball position to minimize poke damage taken","Survive to 6 without falling far behind on CS","Reach 1st item to start contesting her zoning power"],"foe":["Poke you down consistently with ball-enabled trades pre-6","Set up a Shockwave that can flip a skirmish or fight","Snowball early poke damage into lane dominance"]},"early":"Orianna's ball gives her both poke and zoning that outclass your immobile, cooldown-heavy kit in this window, so track her ball's position carefully and avoid standing in its threat range. She wins straightforward trades here, so prioritize safe soldier farming over contesting her directly. Watch for jungle ganks that pair with her ball-slow for a kill setup. Track Command: Shockwave: 110s at rank 1, 80s at rank 3 — it launches you toward the BALL, so track the ball, not her.","mid":"Her ultimate Shockwave is one of the best teamfight tools in the game and can single-handedly flip a fight if she catches your team grouped, so respect her all-in and skirmish potential even after your own R comes online at 6. Your R does give you a way to disengage or wall off her ball's approach, softening the threat. Focus on wave management and safe rotations rather than direct duels in this stretch.","late":"Once you have your first item your poke and clear start to match her ball-based zoning, and by two items your zone control and R give you the tools to counter her Shockwave setup by walling off approach angles or disengaging before she can detonate it. Build MR if she's snowballed a lead (Abyssal Mask), since her burst-and-CC combo remains dangerous in fights. In teamfights, keep your team spread to minimize Shockwave value and use R to block her engage.","whys":["Level 1: Orianna's ball already gives her more consistent poke and zoning than your uncharged soldier trade.","Level 2: Her ball-based pressure continues to chip you down while you lack cooldowns to answer.","Level 3: Her full poke-and-zone kit is online and continues to outtrade your limited early tools.","Levels 4-5: The gap peaks as her ball control lets her punish any positioning mistake severely.","Level 6: Her ultimate Shockwave is a game-deciding teamfight tool, though your own R starts giving you a real answer to her engage.","First item: Your poke and clear finally catch up enough to contest her zoning power directly.","2+ items: Your superior scaling and zone control outclass her more team-oriented kit, flipping extended fights in your favor."]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"pantheon","win":["Pantheon","Pantheon","Pantheon","Skill","Skill","Skill","Azir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Pantheon's Comet Spear poke and Aegis Assault shield let him win nearly every trade and stun-lock you into a kill if he lands his combo — this window is very dangerous."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"His global ultimate threatens a roam-and-kill elsewhere or a devastating dive on you, though your own R gives you a first real answer to his all-in engage."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Nashor's lets your poke punish the 13-second Shield Vault gap, and soldiers zone the walk-up his 575-range spear needs."},{"when":"Late","text":"Your zone control and superior scaling completely outclass his early-game-focused kit, and R shuts down his stun-engage entirely."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive his stun-combo all-in windows without dying pre-6","Avoid pushing the wave into his effective all-in range","Reach 1st item to start out-ranging and out-scaling him"],"foe":["Land Shield Vault stun into a full combo kill","Snowball an early kill into permanent lane dominance","Use his ultimate to affect the map before you can scale"]},"early":"Pantheon's spear poke, shield, and stun combo let him dominate trades against your immobile, cooldown-limited kit, making this one of your harder pre-6 lanes. Avoid pushing the wave into his range and never let him get a free stun off — that combo can end lane on the spot. Play maximally passive, farm safely with W, and ask for jungle attention if he starts snowballing kills.","mid":"His ultimate lets him disappear and either dive you unexpectedly or swing another lane, so ward for his return and respect the all-in threat even after your own R comes online at 6 — R finally gives you a wall to block his jump-in stun combo. Focus on safe farming and side-wave management rather than direct duels in this stretch, since he still wins isolated fights early. Your scaling is the win condition here, not early trades.","late":"Once you have your first item your poke starts punishing his long cooldowns hard, since he has no way to answer at range once you're farmed up, and by two items your zone control and R completely shut down his stun-engage kit — he simply falls off hard past the laning phase. Build early defensive stats (Zhonya's) if he's snowballed a lead, since his combo can still burst you down if unanswered. In teamfights, hold R until he commits his jump, then wall him off from your backline.","whys":["Level 1: Pantheon's spear poke and shield already win trades against your uncharged soldier summon.","Level 2: His stun combo threatens a full trade or kill that you have no way to answer at this stage.","Level 3: His full all-in kit is online and can end lane outright if he lands the stun.","Levels 4-5: This is his peak dominance window — he snowballs hard off any kill while you remain immobile and reactive.","Level 6: His global ultimate adds map pressure and dive threat, though your own R starts giving you a real answer to his engage.","First item: Your poke finally starts punishing his cooldowns hard since he has no ranged answer once you're farmed.","2+ items: Your zone control and scaling completely outclass his early-game-focused kit, flipping the matchup decisively."]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"qiyana","win":["Qiyana","Qiyana","Qiyana","Qiyana","Qiyana","Qiyana","Azir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Qiyana hits 3 first off the back of jungle camp/river element procs and dives you through minions with W dash + E knockup before your soldiers are even summoned reliably."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Her Ultimate lets her blink onto you from brush or river through your wall, so even with Azir R you can get caught before you place a shield-wall reaction."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Once you finish Liandry's/Shard of Truth and hit 2 items you out-scale her burst combo with soldier zoning and E slow at range."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late game your Ultimate splits the map and soldier-wall pokes let you out-position her all-in, since she has no way to close the gap from max range."}],"wants":{"you":["Hold soldiers back and only push with E slow, never let her E-knock you into minions","Buy Cloth Armor/early tenacity item vs her E-Q burst chain","Ward river tri-brush before level 6 so her element-swapped Ult can't blink-flank you"],"foe":["Get river/jungle elemental stacked (rock or grass) before level 3 to burst you down","All-in the instant she sees your soldiers unsummoned or on cooldown","Use Ultimate to blink from an unwarded brush and combo E into R for a full burst kill"]},"early":"Qiyana snowballs the lane by grabbing an elemental rune off jungle camps or river brush and diving you level 3, chaining E knockup into R terrain-stun before your soldiers are up to punish; you're forced to play passively behind minions and just farm what you can with Q poke since her E-W combo out-trades any early stand-and-fight. Track Audacity: 11s at rank 1, 7s at rank 5 — a 650-range dash onto you, and it is not her only one: Terrashape dashes 1100 every 7s.","mid":"By levels 4-5 her combo still one-shots you if she catches a cooldown window, and her Ult lets her blink through fog to flank around your soldier wall, so you keep shoving with W-E to force she to walk up and eat chip damage rather than engaging; level 6 is the exception where your Ult finally lets you disengage and punish her dive with a shieldwall reset.","late":"Once you're 2 items deep your soldier range and E slow outclass her all-in potential entirely — she has no gap-close answer to a fully kited Azir, and teamfights become about you splitting her off Ult while your soldiers zone; the matchup flips hard after laning phase and your win rate climbs even though early game is miserable.","whys":["Level 1 is hers: Royal Privilege front-loads her first hit and Elemental Wrath enchanted off river or brush out-trades a single soldier inside 525.","Level 2 stays hers: Terrashape is a 1100-range dash on a flat 7s, so she picks the range, not you, and two soldiers do not out-trade an enchanted Elemental Wrath.","Shifting Sands completes the safety net at 22s, but Audacity is 11s — she gets two entries for every one escape, and a river-enchanted Q roots you in place for the second.","Levels 4-5 stay hers: every wall and brush re-enchants her weapon, and Audacity is 11s at rank 1 to your 22s Shifting Sands — this is her peak burst window, so drag Qs through her only on last-hits she walks for.","Her all-in threat is still live off any cooldown read at level 6, since Azir's kit hasn't gained enough range/zone control yet to fully punish her engage.","First item does not flip it: Nashor's makes your poke shred, but a 7s Terrashape and an Audacity still choose the fight — shove, rotate, and never stand alone in a side lane.","With 2+ items Azir's split-push and soldier-wall poke fully outclass her lack of a gap-close answer against a kited backline."]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"ryze","win":["Azir","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Azir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Ryze has no way to threaten your soldier-wall poke this early; his Q range and E dash can't close the gap before you've already stacked auto-attacks off two soldiers."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your Ultimate splits the lane and knocks him back, and since Ryze owns no dash his only all-in is a Flash walk-up into Spell Flux — the wall ends it before the root can land."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Both of you spike on first item but your soldier scaling with AP items outpaces his single-target Q-E poke, keeping you ahead on trades even into 2-item Ryze."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late game your zone control with R and W-E combos denies his ability to walk up and root a carry, and unless he's completely ahead in items he can't break your soldier wall to reach backline."}],"wants":{"you":["Punish his low mana early with soldier auto-attack trades before he hits 6","Hold Ultimate for disengage the moment he Flashes in with E-W-Q","Build Shard of Truth/Liandry's to keep soldier range advantage scaling into his tankier build"],"foe":["Farm safely with Q poke and wait for Realm Warp roams to swing side lanes","Stack mana items to spam Q-W-E rotations once he hits a power spike near 2 items","Group early for teamfights where his ult can reposition the whole team"]},"early":"You control this lane from level 1 — Ryze's Overload reaches further than your sand at 1000, but every root he owns stops at 615 and he has no engage tool at all, so you shove with soldiers and force him to farm under tower while you stack CS uncontested; only around level 4 does his mana let the Flux-Overload chain trade back, and even that is a near-even skirmish rather than a real threat.","mid":"Level 6 onward you keep winning trades because your Ultimate knocks back a champion with no dash to re-enter on, and his all-in is a Flash walk-up into Spell Flux that soldier autos punish the instant he commits; the only even window is levels 4-5, when his mana lets the Flux-Overload chain match your rotation, and even there you are not behind.","late":"Late game Ryze wants pick potential and teamfight repositioning via Realm Warp, but your zone control denies him a clean angle to root your backline, and your soldier wall plus R disengage means his all-in still gets punished — this matchup stays comfortably in Azir's favor from lane through the final teamfights, matching the 51.8% win rate.","whys":["Ryze's Overload out-ranges your soldiers at 1000, but he owns no dash and no escape, so any trade that costs him HP costs him the wave as well — you shove him in and deny CS.","Two soldiers up means a real trade: W-Q the drag-through and step back — Rune Prison only slows until Spell Flux is on you, and at level 2 he cannot afford both.","Shifting Sands is your out at 22s and he has no dash to follow it, so greedier soldier placements are fine while his mana pool is still the limit on his poke.","His mana catches up here and the Flux-Overload chain matches your soldier poke spell for spell — the one stage of this lane that is genuinely even.","Azir keeps winning post-6 because Ryze has no gap-closer at all — Realm Warp is a team portal, and the wall knocks him out of his own 615-range chain.","At first item Azir's soldier range and shield scaling continues to outpace Ryze's mana-hungry poke pattern, so the lead compounds rather than resets.","Late game Azir's zone control and disengage deny Ryze the clean root angle he needs on a carry, keeping teamfights in Azir's favor."]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"swain","win":["Azir","Swain","Skill","Skill","Swain","Azir","Azir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Once Swain hits 2 he chains Death's Hand into Nevermove to shred your health bar, and by level 3 that root-and-pull is a real kill threat if you stand still, flipping the trade from your level-1 soldier-poke edge."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Swain's Demonic Ascension drains health from every champion and minion nearby and shortens his Nevermove, so a root inside that 650 radius punishes any over-extension hard."},{"when":"1st item","text":"You're ahead again after first back because your soldier scaling and mobility from W-E lets you disengage his root-heavy kit, while he's still stuck needing to land skillshots to threaten you."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late game your zone control and burst-shield combo out-damages his sustained drain in skirmishes, so you win the split-second trades as long as you don't stand still in his Ult radius."}],"wants":{"you":["Trade cautiously levels 2-5 since his E-Q combo out-damages your early poke","Use soldier mobility to walk out of his Ult drain radius rather than trading through it","Punish his lack of escape once you hit 1st item — he has no dash or blink to disengage"],"foe":["Land Nevermove (E) into Death's Hand (Q) to snowball early trades","Ult and stand in melee/mid range to drain-heal off you and your soldiers","Play for teamfight Ults where his root + drain zone controls entire skirmishes"]},"early":"Level 1 you can poke with soldier autos before he has any threat, but the moment he hits level 2-3 and has Death's Hand bolts plus the Nevermove root, the trade flips hard against you — root-into-bolts out-damages your early kit and forces you to play from max range rather than engaging, making levels 2 through 5 genuinely rough even though you started ahead.","mid":"Level 6 is Swain's biggest spike: his Demonic Ascension heals him massively if you or your soldiers get caught in the radius, so diving or standing to trade is a trap, but the instant you get your first completed item your kiting and soldier zone control let you disengage his slow, immobile kit and start winning trades again cleanly.","late":"Late game Swain has zero mobility to catch a kiting Azir, so as long as you respect his Ultimate's drain radius in skirmishes, your soldier-wall zoning and burst combo win extended trades and teamfights — the matchup nets out roughly even overall with the mid-game window being his best chance to punish you.","whys":["At level 1 Azir's soldier autos outpoke a Swain who has no threat yet, so Azir controls the very start of lane before Torment or drain come online.","Level 2 is his: Death's Hand bolts stack damage per bolt and reach 750 — two soldiers do not out-trade that yet, so hold the poke.","Level 3 is even: Shifting Sands gives you the out, but Nevermove roots on the return from 850 — whoever lands the skillshot, his root or your drag-through, wins the exchange.","The same holds through the rest of that skillshot window — whoever lands Nevermove or the soldier poke cleanly wins the exchange, not raw kit strength.","Swain's Demonic Ascension at 6 heals him massively off anyone caught in the drain radius, making it his single biggest spike and a trap for Azir to trade into.","Once Azir finishes his first item his soldier mobility lets him kite and disengage Swain's rooted, immobile kit, flipping trades back in his favor.","Late game Swain has no mobility to catch a kiting Azir, so respecting the Ult radius lets Azir's zone control and burst win skirmishes."]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"sylas","win":["Sylas","Sylas","Sylas","Sylas","Skill","Skill","Azir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Sylas's Q-E-W chain lets him dash onto you, chain-CC with his own Q, and heal off the damage he deals, out-trading your soldier poke since he closes distance faster than you can kite."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"His Ultimate steals whatever enemy laner's ult he's been fighting, but more importantly his all-in burst combo peaks here — if he's ahead in lane he can force a kill before your soldiers matter."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Even trade window — you've got soldier scaling online but he's got his own first-item burst spike, so it comes down to whoever has priority and positioning."},{"when":"Late","text":"Your zone control and range advantage take over in extended fights since Sylas needs to close distance repeatedly to be effective, and your soldier wall punishes him hard for over-extending."}],"wants":{"you":["Play from max range and never let him land Q-E chain for free","Ward flanks since his all-in relies on catching you out of position","Rush an armor item if he snowballs to blunt his burst-sustain combo"],"foe":["Chain Q-E-W to stunlock and heal through your poke damage early","All-in around level 5-6 when his combo burst peaks before you scale","Look for a stolen Ultimate off another lane to add extra utility to his kit"]},"early":"Sylas's kit is built to dive onto squishy mages and this is exactly that matchup — his Q-E gap close plus self-heal off Petricite Burst lets him tank your soldier poke and still win the trade through levels 3 to 5, so you're forced to play defensively, hold soldiers in reserve, and avoid overextending since a single all-in from him can snowball the lane hard.","mid":"Level 6 is his biggest spike if he's ahead, since his full combo burst plus a stolen Ultimate can end the game right there, but if you've survived to your own level 6 relatively even you finally get the tools — Ultimate shieldwall and disengage — to stabilize the lane and start trading back on your own terms rather than surviving his aggression.","late":"Once teamfights start, your range and zone control finally outclass his need to walk up and land skillshots, and as long as you don't get caught alone by a flanking Sylas your soldier wall punishes his engage attempts hard — the matchup swings back in your favor in extended fights even though laning phase was rough.","whys":["Chain Lash hits twice per cast from 775 and Petricite Burst turns every spell into an empowered swing on the wave — level 1 he trades with your soldier and comes out ahead.","Level 2 stays his: Chain Lash hits twice per cast from 775 and Kingslayer heals the trade back inside 400 — two soldiers do not out-trade that yet.","Shifting Sands is your safety net at 22s, but Kingslayer heals off you every 12s inside 400 and Abscond is 13s — he gets two entries for every escape you have. Still his.","His all-in burst combo peaks right as he gets his last core lane levels, so if he's ahead he can force a kill before Azir's soldiers are numerous enough to matter.","By level 6 Azir finally gets Ultimate shieldwall and disengage tools to stabilize, flipping the lane back in his favor if he survived to this point relatively even.","At first item the fight is genuinely even — Azir's soldier scaling comes online right as Sylas hits his own burst spike, so priority and positioning decide the trade.","Late game Azir's range and zone control outclass Sylas's need to walk up repeatedly, and the soldier wall punishes his engage attempts in extended fights."]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"syndra","win":["Syndra","Syndra","Syndra","Syndra","Skill","Skill","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Syndra's Dark Sphere Q poke plus stun combo out-ranges and out-trades your early soldier zone before you have the mana or item support to answer back consistently."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Unleashed Power fires every sphere she holds on an 80-100 second cooldown, and Splinters of Wrath add an execute on low-health targets — her scariest all-in window."},{"when":"1st item","text":"You start closing the gap here as your soldier scaling and shield utility let you contest her poke without just eating chip damage all game."},{"when":"Late","text":"Your zone control and disengage tools let you out-position her in skirmishes since she has no mobility to reposition once she's committed her stun combo."}],"wants":{"you":["Play passively behind minions early and avoid standing in her stun-sphere combo range","Save Ultimate shieldwall for her all-in windows around level 6","Look to punish her lack of mobility once you have soldier scaling online"],"foe":["Poke relentlessly with Q-E spheres to whittle your HP before she commits","All-in hard the moment she hits level 6 for the Unleashed Power execute","Zone you off farm using orb threat range so you fall behind on CS"]},"early":"Syndra dominates the early trades — her spheres poke from safe range and her stun-into-combo threatens real damage the instant you misstep, so you're forced to farm cautiously behind your own minions and can't contest her zone control until you have levels and items to back up a stand; by level 6 her execute Ultimate makes this her single most dangerous kill window if you're caught low.","mid":"Once you cross into your own 1st-item spike you finally get the tools to trade back — soldier zone denial and a shieldwall disengage blunt her stun-combo all-ins, and from level 6 onward as long as you respect her Ultimate execute threshold you stop bleeding HP for free and start contesting priority.","late":"Late game Syndra has zero escape once she commits her stun combo, so your zone control and range from soldiers let you punish her aggression hard in skirmishes and teamfights — this matchup flips from miserable early lane to comfortably favored in the mid-to-late game, which is why despite a rough laning phase Azir still nets a losing overall win rate against her sustained early pressure.","whys":["At level 1 Syndra's Dark Sphere poke already outranges Azir's undeveloped soldier zone, so she dominates the earliest trades before she has any answer.","Level 2 stays hers: Dark Sphere is a flat 7s and Force of Will flings a sphere or minion from 925 — two soldiers do not out-range that, so hold the poke.","Scatter the Weak lands at 3 and stuns through any sphere she has placed, so the poke-and-stun pattern is live — Shifting Sands is a 22s out and her E is 15s, so trade only once she has spent it.","Levels 4-5 stay hers: Force of Will flings a sphere or minion from 925 and Dark Sphere is a flat 7s, so she out-ranges you and out-chips you — drag Qs through her only on her last-hits.","Emperor's Divide is online: Unleashed Power executes from 675 and Scatter the Weak sets it up, but the wall knocks her out of stun range — with R up you win every 2v2 your jungler joins, and you stop bleeding health for free.","First item: Nashor's turns soldier poke into shred, and you now contest her sphere setup directly instead of absorbing it — shove the crash and make her answer you at soldier range.","Full build she has no mobility once the stun combo is committed — the wall splits her off her team and the soldiers melt a Syndra who cannot leave the sand."]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"taliyah","win":["Taliyah","Taliyah","Taliyah","Taliyah","Taliyah","Azir","Azir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Threaded Volley on Worked Ground plus a Seismic Shove into Unraveled Earth shoves you off farm and sets up the gank before your soldiers scale enough to answer."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Her Ultimate lets her roam the map at will and reposition around walls in fights, but it's less of a direct lane threat than her early Q poke and more of a map-pressure tool."},{"when":"1st item","text":"You start pulling ahead once your soldier scaling and zone control online, since her kit is built for poke and mobility rather than sustained trading against a soldier wall."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late game your range and disengage answer her hit-and-run playstyle, and unless she's snowballed hard off early roams, your zone control wins extended skirmishes."}],"wants":{"you":["Farm from max range under tower early to avoid her Q wave-clear poke","Track her roam timers via her Ultimate — ping side lanes when she leaves","Look to punish her once your soldier scaling and shield combo come online"],"foe":["Spam Q to shove waves and poke you down before you can farm safely","Throw you into Unraveled Earth with Seismic Shove for a free stun","Roam with Ultimate to swing side lanes once she's shoved your lane in"]},"early":"Taliyah's Q wave-clear and poke lets her shove the lane hard and zone you away from CS, and her rock walls both block your soldier pathing and set up easy jungler ganks, so you're on the back foot from level 1 through level 5 just trying to survive lane without falling too far behind on gold and experience. Track Seismic Shove: 14s at rank 1, 8s maxed — the shove into Unraveled Earth is her whole setup, so step up only after it whiffs.","mid":"Her Ultimate at level 6 is more of a roaming and repositioning tool than a lane-kill threat, so this is actually your inflection point — once your soldier zone control and shieldwall come online around your first completed item, you finally answer her poke-and-shove pattern and stop bleeding CS for free.","late":"Late game your range advantage and disengage tools counter her hit-and-run poke playstyle effectively, and as long as she hasn't snowballed a massive lead off early roams, your zone control wins extended teamfights — this matchup is rough in lane but comfortably recoverable if you survive to your own scaling window.","whys":["At level 1 Taliyah's Q wave-clear already shoves the lane and zones Azir off CS before her soldiers can push back.","Level 2 stays hers: Threaded Volley is 7s and clears the wave before two soldiers do, and Seismic Shove throws you out of the trade — poke only after she spends Q.","Shifting Sands completes the safety net at 22s, but Unraveled Earth stuns anything dashing across it on a flat 14s — your one escape runs through her minefield, so level 3 is still hers.","Levels 4-5 stay hers: Threaded Volley is 5s by rank 3 and clears the wave before your soldiers do, so the poke-and-shove pressure holds right up to 6.","Her Ultimate at 6 is a roaming/repositioning tool rather than a lane-kill spike, so she keeps winning lane through map pressure rather than a bigger direct threat.","First item: Nashor's turns soldier poke into shred and you finally clear as fast as she does — shove the crash, take plates, and she stops taking CS for free.","Full build your range and the wall counter her hit-and-run: Weaver's Wall is a roam tool, not a fight-winner, and soldiers melt her the moment she stops to cast."]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"talon","win":["Talon","Talon","Talon","Talon","Talon","Talon","Azir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Rake into an Assassin's Path wall vault drops him on you from brush and bursts your low base HP before soldiers matter, and the vault costs nothing to repeat — his whole early game."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Shadow Assault turns him invisible and converges the blades back through you when he reappears — a 100-second window that opens from fog and finishes the combo."},{"when":"1st item","text":"He's still dangerous but his damage starts falling off relative to your scaling soldiers, and the assassination window narrows since you have more HP and mobility to survive the initial burst."},{"when":"Late","text":"Your zone control and soldier wall finally deny his one-shot assassination pattern in teamfights, since he needs isolation to work and your wall makes picking you off much harder."}],"wants":{"you":["Ward river brush aggressively since his whole kit relies on ambushing from stealth-adjacent positioning","Play extremely safe under tower levels 1-6, never give him an isolated burst window","Rush a defensive item or Zhonya's if he's fed to survive his all-in combo"],"foe":["Vault walls with Assassin's Path to catch you or a side lane early","All-in the instant you're caught out of position or push too far without vision","Snowball off early kills into a lead that lets his burst one-shot you outright"]},"early":"Talon is built to murder exactly this matchup — Rake into an Assassin's Path wall vault drops him on your low base HP from brush, bursts it in one combo, and takes him back out over the same wall before your soldiers can punish him, so from level 1 through level 6 you're playing defensive, warding the river brush, and praying you don't get caught even once, since one mistake means a dead Azir.","mid":"At level 6 Shadow Assault adds invisibility and a second blade pass onto an already lethal combo, so the assassination threat doesn't ease up until you've got real HP and a defensive item to survive the opener — this is one of the roughest lanes in the whole mid pool and you're surviving rather than contesting.","late":"By the time you've stabilized with items, your soldier wall and zone control finally give you the tools to deny his isolation-based assassination pattern in teamfights, but the deficit from laning phase is often too large to fully claw back — this matchup stays rough overall even though the late game narrows the gap somewhat.","whys":["Level 1: Rake hits going out and coming back from 650 and never needs a target — he chips you through the wave and a single soldier cannot answer it.","Level 2 adds Noxian Diplomacy: Rake from 650 into the Q leap, and two soldiers do not out-trade that — poke only after Rake is spent.","Shifting Sands completes the safety net at 22s, but Assassin's Path has no cooldown of its own — he vaults in off any wall, Rake-Q's you, and vaults back out before the dash is back. Still his.","The assassination threat holds all the way to level 6 as well, since his damage output continues to outscale Azir's low-HP squishiness pre-item.","Shadow Assault at 6 adds invisibility and a second blade pass, so he opens the all-in from fog and finishes it from a side you never saw.","At first item Azir's extra HP and soldier presence finally start narrowing the assassination window, though Talon's damage is still meaningfully ahead here.","Once Azir's soldier wall and zone control come online late, they deny the isolation Talon's kit depends on, letting Azir finally win extended fights."]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"twistedfate","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Azir","Twisted Fate","Azir","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Once you hit Level 3 your soldiers out-range TF's Wild Cards poke and you can shove into him under tower without eating free cards, forcing him to farm passively."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"TF's Destiny (R) turns the map inside out — he can vision-lock any sidelane and follow a Gold Card stun with a teleporting gank, so this is his best window to force something even though he's still behind in lane."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your first completed item, Nashor's Tooth, spikes your soldier DPS and wave clear hard, letting you crash and roam off the level-6 window before he can capitalize on Destiny."},{"when":"Late","text":"In teamfights your ultimate (R) zones an entire flank with soldier walls while TF's Destiny is now shared vision utility rather than a duel tool, so you scale into the stronger late-game threat."}],"wants":{"you":["Shove waves fast with Q to deny his card-pickup farming rhythm","Hold E (Shifting Sands) to dash clear the instant he loads a gold-card wind-up","Ping his Destiny cast immediately so your team can play around vision loss"],"foe":["Land the gold card off Pick a Card to stun you before you can wall off","Wait for Destiny to roam and collapse with jungler/support on a sidelane","Poke you down with Wild Cards from max range before you can build soldiers"]},"early":"You out-scale his early poke immediately — TF's Wild Cards do modest damage and his Pick a Card (W) has a long cooldown at low levels, so you can Conquering Sands (Q) soldiers to zone him off the wave without much risk. He has no way to punish your E dash-ins pre-6, and his only real threat is a lucky Gold Card, which you can dodge by never standing still in soldier range.","mid":"Level 6 is his one spike — Destiny gives him global pressure and vision, letting him set up ganks or follow a stun with a teleport-in burst, so respect that timer and don't overextend past minion range around 11-13 minutes. Outside of that window you keep shoving and roaming with your own kit; his damage doesn't scale as cleanly and you can zone his farm with soldier walls whenever he tries to sit on the wave.","late":"By full build your soldiers deal real AoE damage and your ultimate can wall off an entire skirmish, while TF's damage falls off into a support-ish Destiny/Gold Card utility role in fights. Play around your zone control in teamfights, keep him from picking off your backline with Gold Card by holding E for peel, and you close out the game as the stronger scaling threat.","whys":["Azir's ranged soldier zoning outclasses TF's early Wild Cards poke before he has Pick a Card up reliably.","Continued soldier pressure keeps shoving TF off the wave, denying his passive gold generation.","Same story — Azir's wave control and dash mobility keep TF locked out of meaningful trades.","Levels 4-5 stay yours: Nashor's components arrive and the soldier DPS starts to sting, while Pick a Card's gold stun needs him inside auto range — drag Qs through him on every last-hit.","Destiny gives TF global map presence and gank setup that briefly outweighs Azir's lane lead.","Azir's zone control and ultimate wall return to dominating skirmishes once Destiny's initial burst passes.","Full-build Azir out-damages and out-ranges a now-utility-focused TF in late teamfights."]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"veigar","win":["Skill","Skill","Azir","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Veigar's Dark Matter (W) telegraphs but hits hard on a stationary target, so pre-6 trades are close — punish his Event Horizon (E) cooldown after he uses it to escape a soldier shove."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Once you hit Level 6 your ultimate lets you disengage his cage combo or wall him away from the kill, tilting the all-in math firmly in your favor even though Veigar's damage is scary."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your first item, Nashor's Tooth, gives you the poke and clear to punish his slow, immobile farming pattern while his stacking Phenomenal Evil Power is still low — starve the stacks now."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late game Veigar's stacked AP one-shots squishies if he lands Event Horizon, but Azir's soldier walls and R let you break cage setups and protect carries, keeping you ahead if you play around his engage."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait Event Horizon (E) before committing to an all-in, then punish the long cooldown","Use E (Shifting Sands) to dash clear the instant he drops a cage around you","Shove with soldiers to deny his farm — he needs CS/stacks badly to scale"],"foe":["Land Event Horizon around you to cage-lock and follow with Dark Matter + Baleful Strike burst","Farm safely under tower to stack Phenomenal Evil Power for late-game one-shot threat","Wait for you to overextend post-soldier-push so he can flash-cage for a kill"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are close to even — Veigar's Baleful Strike (Q) hits the first two targets in its line and banks permanent AP off every minion it kills, and both champs farm safely from range, but the moment he lands even a partial cage combo it hurts, so treat this as a skill matchup rather than a free lane. By Level 3 your extra soldier and range start winning trades outright as long as you respect his 725-range cage and never dash blind into a walled area.","mid":"Level 4 stays close (his W poke damage scales fast) but your Level 6 ultimate is the swing point — Emperor's Divide lets you wall him out of range or block his cage combo entirely, so all-ins past 6 favor you if you play it out rather than trading blind. Keep shoving to deny his stacks; a starved Veigar mid-game is a non-threat.","late":"He's terrifying with a full stack Event Horizon one-shot combo, but your kit is built to counter exactly that: R disengage, E dash for peel, and soldier zoning to keep him out of cage range on your backline. Play teamfights around denying his flank angle and you remain favored despite his raw burst ceiling.","whys":["Both champions trade roughly evenly at Level 1-2 since Veigar's poke and Azir's soldiers both scale slowly at minimum rank.","Still an even skill matchup — whoever lands Event Horizon or dodges soldiers better wins the exchange.","Azir's extra range and soldier count start to consistently outpace Veigar's short-range poke by Level 3.","Damage racing stays close as Veigar's W scales up, keeping this window a coinflip on positioning.","Azir's Level 6 ultimate gives a hard disengage/wall tool that neutralizes Veigar's all-in, favoring Azir.","Azir's first-item wave clear and poke widen the gap by starving Veigar of his scaling stacks.","Azir's kit is built to disrupt exactly the all-in Veigar needs to convert his late-game power, keeping Azir ahead."]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"vex","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Azir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Doom 'n Gloom (P) fears you and interrupts your E dash whenever it is glowing, and Mistral Bolt (Q) chunks you at 1200 range every time you step up to farm, so early trades favor her."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your Level 6 ultimate is the turning point — Emperor's Divide can wall off her Shadow Surge (R) dash or break the all-in entirely, flipping the lane in your favor for the first time."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Once you finish your first item your soldier clear and poke range let you shove and punish her ground-based mobility kit, since she has no gap closer besides the passive dash-punish."},{"when":"Late","text":"In teamfights your soldier walls and ultimate keep Vex outside Shadow Surge range, while her damage is all skillshot-based and telegraphed, so full-build Azir out-scales and out-controls her."}],"wants":{"you":["Avoid dashing with E near her unless you have to — her passive punishes any dash/blink near her","Play safe and farm with Q soldiers from max range pre-6 to minimize poke exposure","After Level 6, use R to block Doom Bolt or wall her out of an all-in"],"foe":["Bait your E dash or Shifting Sands blink to trigger Personal Space bonus damage","Poke you down with Mistral Bolt and Looming Darkness gloom before you farm","Land Shadow Surge and dash in for a devastating burst before you scale into your own ult"]},"early":"Vex's kit is built to counter exactly what makes Azir dangerous — every dash near her, your E included, marks you for Doom 'n Gloom, and while it glows her next ability fears you outright, so trades and even your escape get punished. She also out-pokes you at 1200 range with Mistral Bolt and stacks Gloom with Looming Darkness, so you farm passively and save E for a real reason.","mid":"The lane flips hard at Level 6 — your ultimate can wall off her Shadow Surge dash or break an all-in combo entirely, which she has no answer for. Before that point stay patient and don't feed her passive with unnecessary dashes; once you have R up you can start contesting her aggression and punishing her when she overextends for poke.","late":"Full build, Azir simply out-scales — soldier walls control zones better than any single skillshot, and your ultimate shuts down her main teamfight tool, the Shadow Surge dash. Vex's damage is real but entirely telegraphed and she has no follow-up mobility once you have R, so play around zoning her out of ult range in fights.","whys":["Mistral Bolt reaches 1200 to your 525 soldier, so she chips at level 1 and you cannot step up to answer.","Continued poke pressure and passive dash-punish keep Vex ahead through this stretch of laning.","Same dynamic — Vex's ranged pressure and anti-mobility passive keep Azir on the back foot pre-6.","Azir is still catching up on gold/XP from playing passively, so Vex retains the edge just before the ult timer.","Azir's Level 6 ultimate finally gives a tool to wall off Vex's all-in and her Shadow Surge dash, flipping the lane.","Azir's item spike adds wave clear and poke that Vex's ground-based kit struggles to answer.","Azir's soldier walls and ultimate shut down Vex's telegraphed burst in teamfights, favoring Azir at full build."]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"viktor","win":["Viktor","Viktor","Viktor","Viktor","Viktor","Azir","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Viktor's Hextech Ray (E) and Gravity Field (W) zone control shut down your soldier positioning early, and he clears waves faster than you can contest, letting him push and bank Hex Fragments unchallenged."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Arcane Storm (R) is a devastating teamfight/skirmish tool with huge zone denial on 120s, but this is where Azir starts closing the gap thanks to soldier count and Emperor's Divide, making the lane closer than before."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Once you complete your first item your wave clear and poke catch up enough to contest his push, though he's still ahead on raw scaling from his Hex Core power spikes."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late game is genuinely close — Viktor's Arcane Storm zones fights hard but Azir's soldier walls and Emperor's Divide provide comparable area control, so this becomes a coinflip decided by positioning and item timing rather than a clean favor either way."}],"wants":{"you":["Avoid standing in Gravity Field zones — losing the fight for space early is costly","Play patient and farm safely rather than contesting Hextech Ray poke pre-6","Look for roams or side-lane pressure since Viktor out-scales your lane presence early"],"foe":["Zone you with Gravity Field (W) then poke freely with Hextech Ray (E) to control the wave","Push Hex Core upgrades on time to keep out-scaling Azir's item timings","Use Arcane Storm to control skirmishes and teamfight positioning once Level 6 hits"]},"early":"Viktor outclasses you in the early lane — Gravity Field denies your soldier zone control, Hextech Ray out-ranges your poke on a 12-second cooldown at rank 1, and his wave clear pushes you under tower repeatedly. Farm at soldier range, poke only on his last-hit steps, and call your jungler once his 17-second W is spent — trading straight up loses until Nashor's Tooth.","mid":"Level 6 brings Arcane Storm online for him on a 120-second cooldown, but this is where your own kit starts to close the gap — soldier count and Emperor's Divide give you comparable area denial for the first time. It's no longer a lost lane, just an even fight where positioning and tracking that 120s matter more than raw stats.","late":"By full items this becomes a genuine skill matchup — Viktor's Arcane Storm and your soldier walls both zone space, and neither side has a clean statistical edge. Bait Hextech Ray out on its 8-second cooldown, track his 80-second ultimate, and use Emperor's Divide to cut his team off from the storm.","whys":["Siphon Power shields him and hits from 600 to your 525 soldier — level 1 he trades and you cannot answer.","Continued Hex Core scaling and wave clear keep Viktor comfortably ahead through this stretch.","Same pattern — Viktor's ranged poke and push power keep Azir on the back foot.","Viktor's scaling power spikes from Hex Core upgrades still outpace Azir's growth heading into 6.","Arcane Storm is a strong standalone teamfight tool that keeps Viktor slightly ahead even as Azir catches up.","Azir's own scaling and item timings finally close the damage/zone-control gap, making this an even fight.","Both ultimates provide comparable zone denial in late fights, making this a genuine coinflip decided by execution."]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"vladimir","win":["Azir","Azir","Azir","Skill","Vladimir","Vladimir","Vladimir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Vladimir has almost no early kill pressure — Transfusion (Q) poke is weak pre-9 and he lacks any hard engage, so your soldiers and range let you shove and zone him off CS freely."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Hemoplague (R) is his one real spike, amplifying damage taken and letting him all-in with Sanguine Pool (W) sustain — respect this window since it's the only point where he can threaten you directly."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your first item narrows things, but Crimson Pact hands Vladimir AP and health from the same purchase — soldier poke stops sticking around here unless you have already bought Grievous Wounds."},{"when":"Late","text":"Full build Vladimir converts every item into both AP and health, so soldier chip stops sticking without Grievous Wounds; your walls buy space in fights but never stop a Sanguine Pool flank onto your carries."}],"wants":{"you":["Shove hard with soldiers pre-6 to deny his passive scaling and force him off CS","Respect Hemoplague timing at Level 6 — don't overextend into his all-in window","Use E to disengage if he pools (W) and tries to reposition for a punish"],"foe":["Farm safely and scale passively until Hemoplague comes online at Level 6","Land Hemoplague on you then follow with Q/E combo for a burst all-in","Use Sanguine Pool to dodge your soldier snap or R ultimate cast"]},"early":"Vladimir has one of the weakest early games in the mid lane — no gap closer, weak poke, and no way to punish your soldier zoning, so you can freely shove waves and deny his farm from Level 1. He's forced to play a passive farming game while you build a substantial CS and XP lead, since he simply doesn't have the tools to contest you in lane.","mid":"Level 6 is his real spike — Hemoplague on 120 seconds amplifies all damage on you and heals him for each champion it hits, so avoid standing forward as it comes up. Keep shoving and denying farm before then; every wave he misses pre-6 is one he cannot convert into the health-and-AP scaling that carries him later.","late":"By full items he is the harder scaler — Crimson Pact doubles every purchase into AP and health, so your soldier chip stops mattering unless you bought Grievous Wounds early. Your walls still buy space, but Sanguine Pool is untargetable for 2 seconds on a 16-second cooldown at rank 5, so keep vision up and never let him pool into your backline unnoticed.","whys":["Azir's soldier zoning and range dominate a Vladimir with no early engage or meaningful poke.","Continued wave control keeps starving Vladimir of the CS and XP he desperately needs to scale.","Same story — Azir's early kit advantage keeps compounding against a passive-scaling Vladimir.","Azir's growing item and level lead widens the gap even further heading into Vladimir's one spike.","Vladimir's Hemoplague finally gives him a real all-in tool, making this his best (though still risky) window.","Crimson Pact turns his items into AP and health at once, out-sustaining Azir's soldier chip damage.","Hemoplague amplifies his team's damage and heals him per champion hit, and a pool-flank ignores Azir's soldier walls."]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"xerath","win":["Xerath","Xerath","Xerath","Xerath","Xerath","Skill","Azir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Xerath's Arcanopulse (Q) at 750 and Shocking Orb (E) stun at 1050 outrange your 525 soldiers, letting him poke you down safely from beyond your engage threat all through the early levels."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Rite of the Arcane (R) adds global siege damage on top of already-dominant poke, making this his peak power window and the hardest point to contest him directly in lane."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your first item finally lets you match his damage output in trades and start punishing his mana-hungry poke pattern, though he's still ahead on raw range."},{"when":"Late","text":"By full build your soldier walls and ultimate let you close the distance and force fights on your terms, while Xerath's stationary poke kit struggles against your mobility and zone control in skirmishes."}],"wants":{"you":["Farm safely from max range and avoid stepping into Arcanopulse/E stun threat range pre-6","Use minion waves as cover to soak poke damage instead of your own health bar","Look to punish him after he uses E stun on a soldier or minion, wasting the cooldown"],"foe":["Poke you down with Arcanopulse and E from max range every wave to force recalls","Land his Shocking Orb (E) stun into a follow-up combo for a lane kill","Use Rite of the Arcane (R) to secure kills across the map or zone objectives"]},"early":"Xerath is one of the most oppressive ranged poke matchups you'll face — Arcanopulse reaches 750 and Shocking Orb 1050 against your 525 soldier, so he chips your health bar every wave with almost no risk of retaliation. Play patient, keep minions between you since both are projectiles, and avoid overextending: Shocking Orb on 13 seconds into his full combo takes a chunk of your health from a distance you can't punish.","mid":"Level 6 is genuinely his strongest window — Rite of the Arcane adds even more poke and siege potential, making this the hardest stretch of the lane to survive. Focus on staying topped off with sustain items and wave management rather than trying to contest him directly; once your own item spike lands you finally start closing the gap.","late":"Full build Azir can finally punish Xerath's stationary poke pattern — your soldier mobility and ultimate let you close distance and force him into uncomfortable positions in skirmishes, while his kit has no answer for sustained pressure up close. Play around vision to avoid his long-range poke in neutral moments, but you're the stronger threat once fights start.","whys":["Xerath's superior range lets him poke Azir down safely before Azir's soldiers can threaten back.","Continued long-range poke keeps Xerath ahead as Azir struggles to close the distance safely.","Same dynamic — Xerath's range advantage compounds through these levels of lane.","Xerath's damage output keeps scaling ahead of Azir's, especially with mana items feeding his poke.","Xerath's ultimate adds global poke on top of an already dominant kit, making this his peak window.","Azir's item spike finally lets him match Xerath's damage and start punishing overextensions.","Azir's mobility and zone control let him force favorable fights against Xerath's stationary kit at full build."]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"yasuo","win":["Yasuo","Yasuo","Yasuo","Skill","Azir","Skill","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Yasuo's Sweeping Blade (E) dashes through your soldiers to close distance instantly, and Last Breath (R) isn't even needed yet — his basic combo of Steel Tempest (Q3) knockup into auto-attacks punishes any soldier you leave hanging out to farm."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your Level 6 ultimate is the turning point — Emperor's Divide can wall off his dash-in engage entirely, denying Sweeping Blade's soldier-hop and forcing him to approach through a much harder angle."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your first item spike widens the gap further, giving you enough poke and soldier presence to zone him out of easy dash range while he's still reliant on landing all-in combos to do damage."},{"when":"Late","text":"In teamfights your ultimate walls off his engage lane entirely, and Last Breath becomes far less threatening when he can't find a soldier or ally to Sweeping Blade through, keeping you ahead at full build."}],"wants":{"you":["Avoid leaving lone soldiers near you that he can Sweeping Blade through to close distance","Use E (Shifting Sands) to reposition the instant he dashes in with Steel Tempest","After Level 6, use R to wall off his engage lane and deny follow-up dashes"],"foe":["Dash through a soldier with Sweeping Blade to close the gap instantly and combo you down","Land Steel Tempest (Q3) knockup then follow with autos and Last Breath for a full combo","Wait near minion waves for a dash target since he has no ranged poke otherwise"]},"early":"Yasuo is genuinely dangerous pre-6 — Sweeping Blade recasts every 0.5 seconds to dash through any soldier or minion, and Wind Wall deletes your soldier attacks and your Q outright for 4 seconds on a 25-second cooldown. Never leave an isolated soldier beside you, poke only once the wall is spent, and keep your dash for escaping rather than entering until your own ultimate answers his engage.","mid":"Level 6 flips the lane hard in your favor — Emperor's Divide can wall off his dash lane entirely, denying the Sweeping Blade engage that makes him so threatening, and forcing him to find a much riskier angle to all-in you. From here you can start contesting him directly and even punishing his aggression instead of just surviving it.","late":"By full build you control the fight — walling off his engage lane with your ultimate neuters Last Breath before it even starts, and your soldier zone control keeps him from finding a clean dash target. He's still dangerous if he flanks or catches a stray soldier, so keep wave management tight and you remain the favored side in skirmishes and fights.","whys":["Steel Tempest is 4s and counts as an auto, so he stacks the knockup on the wave — level 1 he walks up and you cannot push him off.","Continued dash-and-combo pressure keeps Yasuo ahead through this stretch of early lane.","Same dynamic — Yasuo's mobility and all-in combo keep dominating pre-ultimate Azir.","Yasuo's combo threat is still live and punishing careless soldier placement heading into Level 6.","Azir's Level 6 ultimate finally gives a wall to deny Yasuo's dash engage, flipping the lane in Azir's favor.","Azir's item spike and zone control widen the gap further, denying Yasuo easy engage angles.","Azir's ultimate neuters Yasuo's engage lane in teamfights, keeping Azir ahead at full build."]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"yone","win":["Yone","Yone","Yone","Yone","Azir","Skill","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Yone hits level 3 and starts looking for E-Q all-ins through your soldier zone; his knockup dash lets him ignore your spacing tools for one commit and he trades favorably if you're pushed."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Azir's Emperor's Divide ultimate becomes the equalizer — you can wall off his engage or peel a diving Yone off you, and this is the level his all-in stops being free."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Once you finish your first item — Nashor's Tooth into Sorcerer's Shoes — your soldier waveclear and poke damage jump hard, letting you shove and roam while he still has to walk 450 range through sand to reach you."},{"when":"Late","text":"Azir's teamfighting with Arise! armies and a well-placed ultimate wall out-scales Yone's single-target dive, especially if you've kept priority and items."}],"wants":{"you":["Farm from max range behind soldiers, never let him walk you down","Hold E (Shifting Sands) to reposition the instant he flashes in with Q3","Play for level 6 all-in or peel, not earlier trades"],"foe":["Push the wave then E-Q dash in before your soldiers are set","All-in during your cooldowns, especially post-W-Q poke","Force side-lane 1v1s where his mobility ignores your zoning"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are rough — Yone's Q spam and E-in threat force you to play passively and you can't out-damage him in a straight trade; hug your soldiers and don't overextend. It only gets worse levels 3-5 as his knockup dash punishes any greedy cast animation, and his passive crit stacks add up fast if you tunnel farming instead of watching his cooldowns.","mid":"Level 6 flips it: your ultimate wall can block his engage line or displace him mid-dash, and you finally have the burst to punish his all-in instead of just surviving it. From here you want to play the poke-and-zone game, using Conquering Sands to threaten with W-Q combos from max range so he has to walk through soldier damage to reach you.","late":"With items online your waveclear, poke, and ultimate-enabled teamfight presence outscale his single-target dive potential; a well-timed wall splits his team from yours and your soldiers shred anyone caught. Play for sidewaves and group fights where his all-in has to go through your zone control instead of isolating you.","whys":["Yone's early stats and passive crit stacking beat Azir's soft, low-range poke, so you lose the trading window","Level 2 is his: two Mortal Steel stacks turn the third Q into a knock-up dash, so any soldier trade you start ends with you airborne — drag one Q through him and step off","Level 3 is his: Soul Unbound is 22s at rank 1 and that is the window he wants — the spirit dashes through your sand, and the third Mortal Steel knocks you up with no wall to stop it yet.","Still his window: he's one level from getting outscaled but his all-in remains live and dangerous","Azir's ultimate wall arrives and can block or punish his engage, flipping the all-in math to your favor","Your first completed item spikes your poke and clear well past what Yone can punish","With items and your ultimate up, your teamfight and zone control out-scale his dive-heavy kit"]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"zed","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Azir","Skill","Azir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Zed unlocks his full W-E-Q shadow combo and can flash-swap through your soldier zone to burst you before you react, punishing any push."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Azir gets Emperor's Divide, which can wall Zed's Death Mark dash or shove him back mid-combo, but he still has Living Shadow reset to dodge your follow-up so it's a fragile equalizer."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your first item spikes shove speed and poke range, letting you punish his mana-hungry shadow uptime and force him off you before he's ready to all-in."},{"when":"Late","text":"Zed's Death Mark repeats a portion of everything he lands in its 3 seconds, and lethality items make that one rotation lethal if he catches you split from your team, keeping this phase his even into fights."}],"wants":{"you":["Never stand still near minion waves — Zed's shadow swap punishes predictable positioning","Hold E (Shifting Sands) as an escape the second he throws Shadow onto you","Buy an early defensive item (Seeker's Armguard/Zhonya's rush) to survive his level 6 all-in"],"foe":["Shove wave then shadow through it to burst you before minions clear","All-in the moment your E is on cooldown or baited out","Save ultimate for isolated picks past level 6 rather than trading it in lane"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 you're already on the back foot — Zed's shuriken poke plus his level-3 shadow combo threatens your squishy frame, so you play max-range soldier pokes and refuse to overextend. From level 3 through 5 his shadow-assisted burst is fully online while your ultimate isn't, meaning every all-in window is his to take and you're mostly surviving, not winning trades.","mid":"Level 6 gives you Emperor's Divide to wall off his dash or shove him out of range mid-combo — this is your best shot at flipping an all-in, but his Living Shadow swap still lets him bail if it goes wrong, so treat it as parity rather than dominance. Prioritize your first completed item here since the waveclear and poke spike let you punish his cooldowns and control tempo instead of just reacting.","late":"Zed's Death Mark repeats a portion of all damage he lands in its 3 seconds, and lethality items make that one rotation lethal if he isolates you, so this phase stays contested rather than clearly yours. Play around vision and grouping — force him to engage into your soldiers and wall rather than letting him pick you off alone, and treat Zhonya's as mandatory against his all-in burst.","whys":["Zed's early poke and burst threat outclasses Azir's fragile early trading, so the lane opens in his favor","Level 2: Living Shadow lands at 650 and Razor Shuriken from the shadow adds a second 900-range poke — two soldiers can drag one Q through him, then you step off.","Shifting Sands is your out, but Shadow Slash is 5s and Living Shadow 20s — his level 3 combo has two ways in and you have one way out, and no ultimate yet to wall it.","Zed retains the edge at level 5 as his combo damage keeps scaling faster than Azir's kit at this stage","Azir's ultimate wall finally gives a real answer to Zed's engage, flipping this phase in Azir's favor","Zed's lethality item makes Death Mark lethal here, and he can still burst through your shield or isolate you off the wave","With items and positioning discipline Azir's soldier zone and wall control edge out Zed's assassination pattern"]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"ziggs","win":["Ziggs","Ziggs","Ziggs","Ziggs","Skill","Azir","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Ziggs stacks W bombs on the wave and can zone you off farm entirely from beyond your soldier range, forcing you to eat CS losses or risk a stray Q."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Azir's Emperor's Divide gives you an engage/disengage tool that changes the math — you can wall his escape or force him into your soldiers instead of just tanking his poke."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your first item spikes soldier damage and range, letting you finally out-poke his bomb barrage instead of just absorbing it, and start punishing his immobility."},{"when":"Late","text":"Ziggs has zero mobility and Azir's Arise! army plus ultimate wall can trap and burst him from range in teamfights, making this phase clearly yours if you've kept pace on items."}],"wants":{"you":["Farm with soldiers from max range, never walk into his Hexplosive Minefield","Freeze the wave near your tower during levels 3-5 so he can't zone you off CS","Look for all-ins near level 6 and beyond, punishing his complete lack of mobility"],"foe":["Lay Hexplosive Minefield on the wave to zone you off CS and chip you","Poke with Bouncing Bomb whenever you're forced to last-hit","Kite backward and hyper-farm sidewaves he can push safely"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are already tough as Bouncing Bomb's 850 range outpokes your early soldier trades, but it truly bites levels 3-5 when Hexplosive Minefield covers the wave on a flat 16 seconds and threatens a follow-up the instant you step up to farm. Play a freeze near your tower, let minions do the last-hitting, and survive the poke rather than contest it.","mid":"Level 6 is your turning point — Emperor's Divide gives you a wall to cut off his kiting space or force him to engage into your soldiers, something Ziggs's zero-mobility kit has no answer for. From here, prioritize your first item spike to close the poke gap and start punishing his passive playstyle with soldier pressure and roams while he's stuck defending turrets.","late":"With items and your ultimate online, Ziggs becomes easy prey in skirmishes and fights — his total lack of escape means a well-placed wall or a soldier wave can delete him before he gets his own bombs off. Group around objectives and force fights where his immobility is exposed rather than letting him poke from max range behind his own minions.","whys":["Ziggs's bomb range and wave-clear poke outclass Azir's early trading, so the lane opens in his favor","Two soldiers let you drag a Q through him, but Satchel Charge knocks you away on 20s — trade once, then step off","Same story — Ziggs keeps outpoking and outfarming from range while Azir lacks a real answer","Ziggs's zoning advantage persists right up to level 6, still forcing Azir to play passively","Azir's ultimate wall arrives and finally punishes Ziggs's total lack of mobility, flipping the matchup","Azir's item spike closes the poke gap and lets him pressure Ziggs's passive playstyle directly","Ziggs's zero mobility makes him easy pickings for Azir's ranged burst and wall once items are online"]},
  {"a":"azir_mid","b":"zoe","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Azir","Azir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Zoe's Paddle Star into sleepy bubble combo can one-shot you off a single stray minion pickup, and her poke range outclasses your early soldier spacing."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"She still has burst-heavy pick potential post-6 with a completed sheen item, but Azir's Emperor's Divide finally gives you a wall to punish her all-in or block her follow-up."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your first item spike closes the poke gap and lets your soldiers punish her mana-hungry harass pattern, forcing her to play more passively."},{"when":"Late","text":"Azir's Arise! army and ultimate wall give strong teamfight zoning that Zoe's short-range spell-poke kit struggles to answer once you have full item support."}],"wants":{"you":["Never stand near enemy minions Zoe can pick up and throw as bubbles","Play max range with soldiers, refuse short-trades in her poke window","Look to punish her after she spends Q on wave clear, when she's mana-low"],"foe":["Pick up minions with Q to threaten a bubble-sleep bomb combo","Poke relentlessly from range levels 3-5 while you lack an answer","Look for isolated one-shot picks with Sleepy Trouble Bubble setups"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 already favor her poke range, but levels 3-5 are the real danger zone — Zoe's minion-Q pickups threaten a bubble-into-burst combo that can delete you from near-max range, so respect her charge-up animation and never stand near loose minions. She'll out-mana-efficiently harass you off farm repeatedly during this stretch since you have no way to punish her positioning yet.","mid":"Level 6 barely changes her burst threat — she still one-shots with a completed item — but Azir's Emperor's Divide finally gives you a tool to wall her escape route or block a bubble follow-up, making trades slightly less one-sided. Rush your first item here to close the poke gap; once your soldiers hit harder she has to respect your zone instead of freely harassing.","late":"With items and your ultimate online, Azir's teamfight presence — soldier waves plus a well-placed wall — starts to outweigh Zoe's short-ranged, single-target poke kit, especially in grouped fights where she can't isolate a target safely. Play around vision to deny her bubble setups and force fights on your terms rather than letting her snipe from the fog.","whys":["Zoe's poke range and burst combo outclass Azir's early trading, opening the lane in her favor","Her Q-pickup bubble combo threatens a one-shot and Azir has no tool yet to punish or escape it","Same danger continues — her burst window is live and Azir still lacks the ultimate to answer it","Zoe keeps the edge as her spell-poke efficiency continues to outpace Azir's mana-hungry soldiers","She retains a slight edge even at level 6 since her one-shot burst persists with early items","First item: Nashor's turns soldier poke into shred, and a champion whose only escape is a 575-range Portal Jump has to answer you at soldier range — shove the crash and punish her positioning.","Azir's teamfight zoning with soldiers and wall outweighs Zoe's short-range pick potential late"]}
